{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways","id":1001311,"title":"Prohibitive Penalties for Opening Primordial Pathways","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-10T04:51:19-08:00","id":1001311,"title":"Prohibitive Penalties for Opening Primordial Pathways","content":"According to the 'Accessing Your Lair' section, and the really horribly placed and named 'Chambers and Lair Traits' section, the total dice penalty for trying to open a Pathway from a place similar to your chamber (ie, graveyard to graveyard) is -8.<br /> <br /> If you recreate the circumstances under which you formed the original chamber perfectly, it's still -5 (-3 for material world, not the location of chamber, and -2 for Spiritual similarity).<br /> <br /> This is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Are people actually playing with these penalties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T06:45:54-08:00","id":1001336,"title":"","content":"I believe the &quot;Chambers and Lair Traits&quot; and &quot;Accessing Your Lair&quot; sections are talking about two different things. For the latter, the modifiers are for moving between your Lair and a different realm via the Primordial Pathways. The wording in the former is a bit muddied from repeated use of the term &quot;Primordial Pathways,&quot; but refers to imposing Lair Traits on a location that isn't currently resonant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T07:44:38-08:00","id":1001351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001336#post1001336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the &quot;Chambers and Lair Traits&quot; and &quot;Accessing Your Lair&quot; sections are talking about two different things. For the latter, the modifiers are for moving between your Lair and a different realm via the Primordial Pathways. The wording in the former is a bit muddied from repeated use of the term &quot;Primordial Pathways,&quot; but refers to imposing Lair Traits on a location that isn't currently resonant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my initial reading as well, but I can't fathom why it would explicitly call out the term opening a Primordial Pathway if it was only talking about Lair Traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T08:01:31-08:00","id":1001355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001351#post1001351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my initial reading as well, but I can't fathom why it would explicitly call out the term opening a Primordial Pathway if it was only talking about Lair Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It certainly feels like an editing mistake given the position of the section as you mentioned. I will be running it as Chambers and Lair Traits is for imposing traits only, and the 'Accessing Your Lair' section will be for Primordial Pathways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T08:07:12-08:00","id":1001359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways#post1001311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the 'Accessing Your Lair' section, and the really horribly placed and named 'Chambers and Lair Traits' section, the total dice penalty for trying to open a Pathway from a place similar to your chamber (ie, graveyard to graveyard) is -8.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea. Lair Traits and/or being Gorged serve to offset those penalties and Beasts are pretty strongly incentivized to funnel their Experiences into Attributes in the first place.<br /> <br /> The mechanical intent of the Pathways has never been to shortcut to places with only a tangential relation to your Legend and if you intent to use your Lair to get around a lot you're encouraged to develop Traits that are persistent or easy to recreate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T08:33:57-08:00","id":1001367,"title":"","content":"Opening a pathway from a location other than the one corresponding to the target chamber is nigh-impossible for a starting beast and utterly trivial for one at Lair 10, where the presence of any of their 7 lair traits lets them impose the other 6 and drag the penalty down to -1. Most characters will find them somewhere between these two extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:20:45-08:00","id":1001486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001367#post1001367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opening a pathway from a location other than the one corresponding to the target chamber is nigh-impossible for a starting beast and utterly trivial for one at Lair 10, where the presence of any of their 7 lair traits lets them impose the other 6 and drag the penalty down to -1. Most characters will find them somewhere between these two extremes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was meant to be required, I feel like the example should have been a lot more involved than the sample Beast running into a location with mere descriptive similarity and calling down a Pathway on the first try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T16:59:31-08:00","id":1001547,"title":"","content":"It's an example. Making it too involved would have been confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T20:35:26-08:00","id":1001610,"title":"","content":"The entire Chamber and Lair Traits section doesn't make a whole lot of sense, honestly. It's supposed to provide a way to impose Traits without finding or creating one naturally, but if an area has a strong physical resemblance to one of your Chambers it probably has at least one of those Traits already, rendering the whole penalty/satiety expenditure thing moot. It also doesn't clarify if the penalties are supposed to work both ways, exiting the Lair to a location in the material world doesn't have any coverage in that section. If resonance really is the key factor then you're pretty stuck. It's not even possible to achieve narrative or spiritual similarity, or to impose any of your Traits that aren't prexisting, on the external end being as you're in the Lair until you succeed on the roll. That leaves Beasts in the Lair with huge penalties and no way to mitigate them, which I doubt is the intent.<br /> <br /> I just ignore that section and use the bar for Accessing the Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T20:45:56-08:00","id":1001611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001486#post1001486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was meant to be required, I feel like the example should have been a lot more involved than the sample Beast running into a location with mere descriptive similarity and calling down a Pathway on the first try.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Tries to do the thing&quot; means &quot;does the thing on the first try&quot; now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001610#post1001610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire Chamber and Lair Traits section doesn't make a whole lot of sense, honestly. It's supposed to provide a way to impose Traits without finding or creating one naturally, but if an area has a strong physical resemblance to one of your Chambers it probably has at least one of those Traits already, rendering the whole penalty/satiety expenditure thing moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a Chamber that you formed in Blizzard conditions or during a Darkness-inducing blackout isn't going to make any given abandoned shack resonant by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also doesn't clarify if the penalties are supposed to work both ways, exiting the Lair to a location in the material world doesn't have any coverage in that section. If resonance really is the key factor then you're pretty stuck. It's not even possible to achieve narrative or spiritual similarity, or to impose any of your Traits that aren't prexisting, on the external end being as you're in the Lair until you succeed on the roll. That leaves Beasts in the Lair with huge penalties and no way to mitigate them, which I doubt is the intent. </div> </div> </div>No, that's absolutely the intent. The point is to spread your Legend to places that are similar to your existing Chambers so that you establish shortcuts and waypoints, not to be able to freely jump into anybody's home just because you have a house-based Chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T23:21:00-08:00","id":1001644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001611#post1001611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Tries to do the thing&quot; means &quot;does the thing on the first try&quot; now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're disputing that the immense difficulty of doing something like this isn't accurately represented, I don't understand why you're pushing this angle. The example doesn't accurately represent the actual process, and makes it look like the intent is, in fact, to be able to open pathways with relative ease in locations that are similar to your Lair. The entire section of expanded penalties isn't even included in the section about pathways (it's shoved in with Lair traits), and reads like an editing artifact from when the system worked differently.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I respect your ability to parse ChroD rules, and I can absolutely accept that you're right - this is probably intended.<br /> <br /> Part two of this question: do you have actual play experience using these penalties? Does anyone that's supporting them here have actual play experience with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:23:52-08:00","id":1001655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001644#post1001644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're disputing that the immense difficulty of doing something like this isn't accurately represented, I don't understand why you're pushing this angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're conflating the recurrent Eshmaki-in-a-pine-forest example with the Anakim-in-the-abandoned-school-that-is-their-Chamber-seed example of simply opening a Pathway, there's no reason to mention try-count at all, which is a point of legitimate confusion irrespective of the way the penalties are arranged in the book.<br /> <br /> Opening a Pathway is an Attribute task whose greatest utility in circumstances where high penalties can't be offset (due to lack of preparation and/or power) is buying a few turns of acting with the full strength of your Horror, which necessarily serves as a reason to limit its chance of success and duration of effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:43:22-08:00","id":1001659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001655#post1001655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anakim-in-the-abandoned-school-that-is-their-Chamber-seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually didn't realize the school in question was his seed. I'm really glad you pointed that out.<br /> <br /> I'd still like to hear from anyone that has experience with these in actual play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:54:35-08:00","id":1001699,"title":"","content":"I generally assume the -3 for getting out when you don't really care where in the destination realm you end up covers the similarity factors. Aside form that you either need cooperation from brood members (they can all impose one of your lair traits on an area) or just exit via your real-world chamber analogues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:13:35-08:00","id":1001849,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> has convinced me that it is intended to be both, and I think that it is thematically appropriate for it to work the way he says. That being said, I don't yet know how that actually plays out in game as far as difficultly goes and I still think that the editing isn't then best (granted, I think that about the whole book; I think mostly caused by the Kickstarter backlash and re-working).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:02:31-08:00","id":1002090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1001699#post1001699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally assume the -3 for getting out when you don't really care where in the destination realm you end up covers the similarity factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the implicit ability to technically narrow the field of random results with Lair Traits justifies keeping the penalty for descriptive similarity; it makes blind shortcutting jaunts across the world more likely to wear out your Willpower or strain your Lair to the breaking point than to succeed until you've got some experience under your belt while still allowing for informed cross-continental movement with only the penalties for realm and resonance to worry about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T01:00:21-08:00","id":1002150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002090#post1002090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the implicit ability to technically narrow the field of random results with Lair Traits justifies keeping the penalty for descriptive similarity; it makes blind shortcutting jaunts across the world more likely to wear out your Willpower or strain your Lair to the breaking point than to succeed until you've got some experience under your belt while still allowing for informed cross-continental movement with only the penalties for realm and resonance to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you clarify what you mean here?<br /> <br /> Would it be possible to choose a 'random' location, but one that's under the effect of some of your traits to receive the bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T03:12:20-08:00","id":1002167,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the idea is that if you just blindly jump you'll probably end up in a place with one or more of your lair traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T09:12:53-08:00","id":1002243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002150#post1002150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you clarify what you mean here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having that -5 penalty for descriptive similarity still apply to random jumps makes it more likely that you'll fail or dramatically fail, and only going &quot;somewhere in the Underworld that's a forest with a lot of Stinging Swarms and Rotting Undergrowth,&quot; for example, is generally liable to put you farther from the relative safety of a given realm's less extreme shallows \u2014 plunging headfirst into the kind of place that may well have a minor god or three hanging around is more likely to get you into trouble than out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it be possible to choose a 'random' location, but one that's under the effect of some of your traits to receive the bonus? </div> </div> </div>That's the hypothesis. The fact that it's easier to feel your way into other realms lessens the utility of &quot;jump to a Jagged Burning Flooded Electrified lakeside cabin&quot; as a quick travel tool, but after the first trip the -3 goes away and the greater degree of pre-established groundwork means you can try your hand at building out from there at a more measured pace, as opposed to, say, trying to hop straight from one material-world church to another solely on the basis of shared churchness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:38:20-08:00","id":1002315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002243#post1002243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having that -5 penalty for descriptive similarity still apply to random jumps makes it more likely that you'll fail or dramatically fail, and only going &quot;somewhere in the Underworld that's a forest with a lot of Stinging Swarms and Rotting Undergrowth,&quot; for example, is generally liable to put you farther from the relative safety of a given realm's less extreme shallows \u2014 plunging headfirst into the kind of place that may well have a minor god or three hanging around is more likely to get you into trouble than out.<br /> <br /> That's the hypothesis. The fact that it's easier to feel your way into other realms lessens the utility of &quot;jump to a Jagged Burning Flooded Electrified lakeside cabin&quot; as a quick travel tool, but after the first trip the -3 goes away and the greater degree of pre-established groundwork means you can try your hand at building out from there at a more measured pace, as opposed to, say, trying to hop straight from one material-world church to another solely on the basis of shared churchness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this has been super helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:02:30-08:00","id":1002322,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, and everyone else, could a Beast open the pathway while using Soul Communion, as their Horror? The book mentions that Horrors are capable of opening them, but has nothing to say on this particular subject. It seems like they should be able to - and take advantage of the Horror's potentially larger dicepool - but if they <i>can</i>\u200b, I don't see any reason why they would ever choose not to, which I guess may or may not be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:46:48-08:00","id":1002368,"title":"","content":"The problem with keeping the penalty for how similar the location is on a random jump is that it's a <i>random</i> jump. <i>So</i> <i>you don't know what that is.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:35:04-08:00","id":1002426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002368#post1002368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with keeping the penalty for how similar the location is on a random jump is that it's a <i>random</i> jump. <i>So</i> <i>you don't know what that is.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It is de facto either the maximum possible malus or the vanishingly minuscule chance that there is a <i>perfectly identical location</i> somewhere in the world that you can reach with your Lair, because all the intervening levels require you to have been to the place before and done something there by definition and therefore have no real business trucking with the random-draw penalty in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002322#post1002322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, and everyone else, could a Beast open the pathway while using Soul Communion, as their Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to treat the Pathway as using a consistent dicepool that doesn't get bigger in the Lair, because the nearest mechanical analogue to the Horror opening a Pathway on its own is the Power + Lair roll from Inflicting Nightmares (which uses neither equivalent of the normal roll's base Attributes) and because as near as I can piece together from how Be My Guest could conceivably work the ability to readily open Pathways to non-Chamber locations and trivially add bonus dice through Lair Trait imposition is already a substantial advantage the Begotten have over any other monster trying to use the Pathways.<br /> <br /> The question of whether you can be in one location and have your Horror occupy an irrelevant Chamber to open a Primordial Pathway to another location that you're not in is a little less easily pieced together, because while there's a case to be made for it in theory and it makes for a neat bit of spooky-action-at-a-distance there's no examples of it on the books so far and it would dramatically extend the reach of any given Beast despite the importance the splat's mechanics generally place on being physically present. More content is needed to answer this angle on the question, and with any luck the Player's Guide or the Storyteller's Guide will give us something to work from in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T07:21:54-08:00","id":1002519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002426#post1002426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> all the intervening levels require you to have been to the place before and done something there by definition</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't. If you're in a chamber formed by a breaking point due to the supernatural then finding a spiritually similar one should be a piece of cake. Any breaking point at all could technically qualify for Narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T17:40:29-08:00","id":1002718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002519#post1002519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any breaking point at all could technically qualify for Narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. If the example's distinction between narrative and spiritual similarity is &quot;you carry out the same process but do not produce the same Chamber-generating effect,&quot; then the point of similarity for secondhand Chambers is, at best, &quot;the same supernatural being or a very faithful copycat carried out the same process,&quot; and if you've taken the time to research the supernatural being that created one of your Chambers then you very probably have an idea of where else it's been active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T00:41:45-08:00","id":1002794,"title":"","content":"Or someone experiences the same <i>regular</i> breaking point that allowed a beast to create the chamber because they were there, when they aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:04:14-08:00","id":1002967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002794#post1002794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or someone experiences the same <i>regular</i> breaking point that allowed a beast to create the chamber because they were there, when they aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition, that runs it out of the realm of narrative similarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:07:13-08:00","id":1002970,"title":"","content":"How so? The same thing happens, but for the crucial part that allowed a chamber to form. How is that not narratively similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:34:40-08:00","id":1002980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002970#post1002970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? The same thing happens, but for the crucial part that allowed a chamber to form. How is that not narratively similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chambers form from the presence of a Lair Trait in combination with either exceptional successes on Nightmare rolls, the presence of a Beast for a breaking point suffered by a being with Integrity or a suitable equivalent Trait, or the loss of Integrity by a human character due to a meeting with the supernatural. This last option is the one that produces Chambers with an explicit expiration date, so by implication the other two have an arbitrary shelf life but keep their utility as sources of resonance if they align with an existing Chamber.<br /> <br /> You may notice that it's only the involved of a Beast that allows the other two methods of Chamber integration to work and that Begotten involvement provides the best chance you have for integrating a Chamber without a personal connection to one or both participants in its formation.<br /> <br /> You may also notice that the examples for spiritual and narrative similarity are <i>only</i> distinguished by the metaphysical component that forms a Chamber. <i>If you haven't hunted someone through the pine forest, it doesn't matter if they had a breaking point there, because the narrative resonance is<b> &quot;you hunted someone through a pine forest.&quot;</b></i> Spiritual resonance only tacks on &quot;and they suffered a breaking point/you got an exceptional success on invoking a Nightmare&quot; as an additional qualifier.<br /> <br /> Beasts use the Pathways through their Legends being tied to a location. Their Legends by necessity involve them personally or by preestablished ties in the collective unconscious, and if someone suffered a breaking point there and no Beast or other supernatural being was involved, there's no connection to <i>anybody's</i> Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:13:32-08:00","id":1003056,"title":"","content":"A myth eater's gonna be pretty miffed if there ain't no myth to eat.<br /> <br /> I make no apologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:03:09-08:00","id":1003118,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and if you formed a chamber because you saw someone murder a dude, the narrative resonance is &quot;<b>someone murdered a dude</b>&quot;. No beast necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:23:18-08:00","id":1003125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003118#post1003118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and if you formed a chamber because you saw someone murder a dude, the narrative resonance is &quot;<b>someone murdered a dude</b>&quot;. No beast necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside how &quot;someone murdered a dude&quot; is a &quot;narrative&quot; that has at least four wildly different processes that come to mind immediately which all paint different pictures, the Temenos (and by extension the Primordial Dream) doesn't truck so well with &quot;three can keep a secret if two of them are dead&quot; without the involvement of a party that only has the part of the human soul that corresponds to the wider collective elements.<br /> <br /> The narrative resonance is &quot;a Beast was present for someone losing Integrity in the process of a murder by [method],&quot; not &quot;someone murdered a dude.&quot; Murder having nigh-inherent narrative weight does not make the act alone a narrative unto itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:32:10-08:00","id":1003129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002980#post1002980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chambers form from the presence of a Lair Trait in combination with either exceptional successes on Nightmare rolls, the presence of a Beast for a breaking point suffered by a being with Integrity or a suitable equivalent Trait, or the loss of Integrity by a human character due to a meeting with the supernatural. This last option is the one that produces Chambers with an explicit expiration date, so by implication the other two have an arbitrary shelf life but keep their utility as sources of resonance if they align with an existing Chamber.<br /> <br /> You may notice that it's only the involved of a Beast that allows the other two methods of Chamber integration to work and that Begotten involvement provides the best chance you have for integrating a Chamber without a personal connection to one or both participants in its formation.<br /> <br /> You may also notice that the examples for spiritual and narrative similarity are <i>only</i> distinguished by the metaphysical component that forms a Chamber. <i>If you haven't hunted someone through the pine forest, it doesn't matter if they had a breaking point there, because the narrative resonance is<b> &quot;you hunted someone through a pine forest.&quot;</b></i> Spiritual resonance only tacks on &quot;and they suffered a breaking point/you got an exceptional success on invoking a Nightmare&quot; as an additional qualifier.<br /> <br /> Beasts use the Pathways through their Legends being tied to a location. Their Legends by necessity involve them personally or by preestablished ties in the collective unconscious, and if someone suffered a breaking point there and no Beast or other supernatural being was involved, there's no connection to <i>anybody's</i> Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, under this interpetation, would the third chamber type even be possible to open a Pathway to?<br /> <br /> I also think that by RAW, Elfive is right. But RAI may have meant for there to be more tight thematics here as you suggest.<br /> <br /> Weren't the non-Beast created Chambers added after the initial Kickstarter draft was released?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:38:35-08:00","id":1003130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003125#post1003125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative resonance is &quot;a Beast was present for someone losing Integrity in the process of a murder by [method],&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the beast being present is what qualifies it for a chamber, so that's the <i>spiritual</i> resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:39:56-08:00","id":1003131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003129#post1003129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, under this interpetation, would the third chamber type even be possible to open a Pathway to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Under this interpretation, similar locations where the same supernatural being or other monsters duplicated the process would be fair game (think Darius and Darius); Beasts who make heavy use of Family Dinner and/or exert their influence over a supernatural bloc get a lot out of that method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weren't the non-Beast created Chambers added after the initial Kickstarter draft was released? </div> </div> </div>They weren't in the first draft, correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003130#post1003130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because the beast being present is what qualifies it for a chamber, so that's the <i>spiritual</i> resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>breaking point</i> is the distinction between narrative and spiritual resonance, else the example would have &quot;the Eshmaki gets an exceptional success on her Nightmare roll without stalking the victim through the woods&quot; as the narrative resonance equivalent of &quot;the Eshmaki stalks a victim through the woods and gets an exceptional success on her Nightmare roll&quot; instead of &quot;the Eshmaki stalks a victim through the woods but doesn't get an exceptional success on her Nightmare roll.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-14-2016, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T17:53:43-08:00","id":1003169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003131#post1003131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>breaking point</i> is the distinction between narrative and spiritual resonance, else the example would have &quot;the Eshmaki gets an exceptional success on her Nightmare roll without stalking the victim through the woods&quot; as the narrative resonance equivalent of &quot;the Eshmaki stalks a victim through the woods and gets an exceptional success on her Nightmare roll&quot; instead of &quot;the Eshmaki stalks a victim through the woods but doesn't get an exceptional success on her Nightmare roll.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're looking too hard at the example and not hard enough at the rules. The beast stalking in the forest is a very active example of chamber creation. In a passive one such as the beast simply witnessing a breaking point there's two avenues for &quot;the same thing happens but no chamber gets formed&quot;. One is the lack of the breaking point, the other is the lack of the beast. They BOTH count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-14-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:13:09-08:00","id":1003231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003169#post1003169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're looking too hard at the example and not hard enough at the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking at &quot;an ability to use your connection to the collective unconscious of humanity through the narrative that builds up around the monster you are works better than the baseline if you cause the circumstances that bound a location to that narrative to be repeated in a similar location with varying levels of success&quot; and determining that something goofy is happening if you are able to hop to an unremarkable poorly-lit parking garage as easily as a poorly-lit parking garage in which one person strangled another to death and shed a piece of their self-image through the use of the fact that you saw somebody strangle somebody else to death in a poorly-lit parking garage and have a breakdown once and decided to incorporate this scene into the landscape of your soul despite that being something you can only do once in a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The beast stalking in the forest is a very active example of chamber creation. In a passive one such as the beast simply witnessing a breaking point there's two avenues for &quot;the same thing happens but no chamber gets formed&quot;. One is the lack of the breaking point, the other is the lack of the beast. They BOTH count. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The confrontation with the Primordial Dream that allowed for the Chamber,&quot; i.e. &quot;the prerequisite for expanding the Lair,&quot; is the explicit distinguishing element between spiritual similarity and mere narrative similarity. The prerequisite that is not &quot;the place came close to the Primordial Dream because a Beast did really well at using a power that pulls the Primordial Dream close to a place&quot; is &quot;a Beast was present for a breaking point and therefore provides that breaking point with a metaphysical association to the Primordial Dream.&quot;<br /> <br /> Assorted other mechanics relating to the Begotten emphasize the necessity of being physically present for an event or at least having a personal understanding of it to gain benefit from it, and the Temenos doesn't pick stuff up that's not both currently shared between multiple people and possessed of strong resonance. The Begotten sidestep the latter part by virtue of personally being potent chunks of the collective unconscious and shortcut the former thanks to their not having a personal dreamscape that's distinct from the dreamscape of all humanity, but there's not otherwise a reason for a murderer's loss of Integrity to be relevant to humanity's communal brainspace without one of the Children present to catch it on record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-15-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:50:55-08:00","id":1003295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003231#post1003231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but there's not otherwise a reason for a murderer's loss of Integrity to be relevant to humanity's communal brainspace without one of the Children present to catch it on record.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is. There totally is. You've got a monster that is known to habitually stalk a place where this gruesome murder once happened, and if you commit a similar murder in a similar place there's a small chance the act will <i>summon it. </i><br /> <br /> That's a thing. That is <i>definitely</i> a thing. You cannot argue that that is not a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:40:21-08:00","id":1003384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003131#post1003131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under this interpretation, similar locations where the same supernatural being or other monsters duplicated the process would be fair game (think Darius and Darius); Beasts who make heavy use of Family Dinner and/or exert their influence over a supernatural bloc get a lot out of that method.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was reffering to, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> is, the case where the chamber is formed independently of a Beast who then comes upon it later and adds it to their Lair at the time. They have never met the Supernatural that caused the Chamber in this example. If there is an alleyway where a vampire feeds and a chamber forms off of it, a Beast can add that Chamber to their Lair after encountering the Chamber or its physical location. By RAW, that Beast could then use a different but similar alleyway where another vampire feeds on another person to open a pathway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003131#post1003131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They weren't in the first draft, correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think that your interpertation is wonderfully thematic and will likely use it myself, it doesn't seem that all the sections were taken into account when the non-Beast Chamber creation was added. Which leads to a bit of dissonance here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:16:38-08:00","id":1003463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003295#post1003295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is. There totally is. You've got a monster that is known to habitually stalk a place where this gruesome murder once happened, and if you commit a similar murder in a similar place there's a small chance the act will <i>summon it. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the connection to the narrative.<br /> <br /> That pretty much <i>only works for people who know about that monster.</i><br /> <br /> The Watcher of Boston watching a murderer lose himself in a darkened alley does not make a darkened alley where a murderer lost himself in Osaka any more relevant to the Watcher of Boston than any other darkened alley if neither the Watcher of Boston nor her Legend have been present or heard of in Osaka.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003384#post1003384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reffering to, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> is, the case where the chamber is formed independently of a Beast who then comes upon it later and adds it to their Lair at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elfive's argument currently appears to concern the &quot;Beast is present for a breaking point&quot; method through the idea that narrative similarity doesn't still key off the idea that being present at an event that plays out similarly to an event you witnessed to form a Chamber is still part of the narrative role of that Chamber's formation. No other supernatural beings need be involved in that method of Chamber creation, but a Beast does need to be present for that breakdown of self-image to be relevant to the formation of a Chamber or the conscious use of that location as a destination via the Pathways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have never met the Supernatural that caused the Chamber in this example. If there is an alleyway where a vampire feeds and a chamber forms off of it, a Beast can add that Chamber to their Lair after encountering the Chamber or its physical location. </div> </div> </div>Well, no, that's explicitly not how adding a secondhand Chamber works. There's a whole system for finding out what happened to form a Chamber and who/what was involved that you need to go through first that gets substantially easier the more relevant you are to the participants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By RAW, that Beast could then use a different but similar alleyway where another vampire feeds on another person to open a pathway. </div> </div> </div>They could use a similar alleyway anyway. They're not going to be getting any better than descriptive similarity on the Pathway roll without a substantially lucky confluence of events on a random jaunt, but the ability to pick a random location you've never been to in the mortal world that happens to meet the basic description of one of your Chambers and try to jump there without at least hunting there first doesn't have any inherent reliance on your Legend.<br /> <br /> If another vampire feeds on a mortal <i>in the same fashion</i>, i.e. causing a breaking point through exposure to the supernatural, feeding on the same type of subject/through the same area/etc, such that you could readily compare that Chamber's formation to that of the one in your Lair, then you could angle for one of the intermediate resonance levels, but again, the likelihood of a monster replicating the activities of another monster it's never encountered even by reputation is substantially small.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:03:38-08:00","id":1003488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003463#post1003463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elfive's argument currently appears to concern the &quot;Beast is present for a breaking point&quot; method through the idea that narrative similarity doesn't still key off the idea that being present at an event that plays out similarly to an event you witnessed to form a Chamber is still part of the narrative role of that Chamber's formation. No other supernatural beings need be involved in that method of Chamber creation, but a Beast does need to be present for that breakdown of self-image to be relevant to the formation of a Chamber or the conscious use of that location as a destination via the Pathways.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit that I may have mischaracterized Elfive's points, I'll just concentrate on my own instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003463#post1003463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, no, that's explicitly not how adding a secondhand Chamber works. There's a whole system for finding out what happened to form a Chamber and who/what was involved that you need to go through first that gets substantially easier the more relevant you are to the participants.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is how it works though. Yes, you have to go through the process and such. And yes it gets easier the more connected you are. But you don't HAVE to know the supernatural that caused it nor be present for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003463#post1003463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could use a similar alleyway anyway. They're not going to be getting any better than descriptive similarity on the Pathway roll without a substantially lucky confluence of events on a random jaunt, but the ability to pick a random location you've never been to in the mortal world that happens to meet the basic description of one of your Chambers and try to jump there without at least hunting there first doesn't have any inherent reliance on your Legend.<br /> <br /> If another vampire feeds on a mortal <i>in the same fashion</i>, i.e. causing a breaking point through exposure to the supernatural, feeding on the same type of subject/through the same area/etc, such that you could readily compare that Chamber's formation to that of the one in your Lair, then you could angle for one of the intermediate resonance levels, but again, the likelihood of a monster replicating the activities of another monster it's never encountered even by reputation is substantially small.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was being brief about it, but yes I was presuming that the breaking point and method/details of feeding were the same. You have admitted it here, it may not be likely or easy but it is possible as written to open a pathway in this situation.<br /> <br /> To help the situation be less far-fetched I would posit that you could <i>purposefully</i> have a vampire friend recreate the scene for you based on how you determined your Chamber was formed. This isn't for completely random jumps to the physical world but is a thing that can be done.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:09:53-08:00","id":1003491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003488#post1003488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is how it works though. Yes, you have to go through the process and such. And yes it gets easier the more connected you are. But you don't HAVE to know the supernatural that caused it nor be present for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You explicitly need to learn what supernatural being was involved in the creation of the Chamber before you can add it to your Lair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was being brief about it, but yes I was presuming that the breaking point and method/details of feeding were the same. You have admitted it here, it may not be likely or easy but it is possible as written to open a pathway in this situation. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's not under contention. &quot;It's impossible&quot; was never my point. My point is that you're not getting any better than descriptive similarity for Chamber resonance on a random jump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:22:40-08:00","id":1003497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003491#post1003491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You explicitly need to learn what supernatural being was involved in the creation of the Chamber before you can add it to your Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Learn <i>about </i>them yes, that doesn't mean you have to know them though. It is left a bit to storyteller discretion where the line is but it certainly doesnt imply that you have to know them or have been there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003491#post1003491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's not under contention. &quot;It's impossible&quot; was never my point. My point is that you're not getting any better than descriptive similarity for Chamber resonance on a random jump.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did say impossible though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1002426#post1002426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is de facto either the maximum possible malus or the vanishingly minuscule chance that there is a <i>perfectly identical location</i> somewhere in the world that you can reach with your Lair,<b> because all the intervening levels require you to have been to the place before and done something there by definition</b> and therefore have no real business trucking with the random-draw penalty in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> That is the exact line that Elfive quoted that started this whole bit of discussion. The contention is that said levels do not <b>require</b> you to have been there as you said here, though it certainly helps. It could happen on a random jump, however unlikely, if it meets the needs of the story.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:59:32-08:00","id":1003524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003497#post1003497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Learn <i>about </i>them yes, that doesn't mean you have to know them though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your initial framing suggested that you thought there was no preamble to adding a secondhand Chamber beyond coming across the Chamber, which was the source of my &quot;Well, no.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is left a bit to storyteller discretion where the line is but it certainly doesnt imply that you have to know them or have been there. </div> </div> </div>You specifically have to have been there to add the Chamber and I was not suggesting knowledge of the inciting monster in the sense of acquaintance; you don't <i>need</i> to be friends with the vampire that formed a Chamber to incorporate it, but you do need to know how they caused a mortal to suffer a breaking point and how that vampire is distinguished from other vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You did say impossible though: </div> </div> </div>In the context of &quot;you are consciously reaching for a random [location-type analogous to one of your Chambers],&quot; yes, you are not going to have the necessary knowledge of a random location to be able to angle for the ease of transport which comes from having a specific narrative associated with both you and your destination point.<br /> <br /> You're not going to be able to exploit the fact that somebody was tortured/was subject to a powerful Nightmare/encountered a monster in a <i>random location</i> through the fact that you're in a Chamber based on that kind of location.<br /> <br /> You <i>could</i>, however, jump to a Chamber that formed in that location substantially more readily than you could to the material roots of it, because there's a whole four dice of difference between a -3 penalty and a +1 bonus irrespective of resonance penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:13:40-08:00","id":1003561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003524#post1003524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your initial framing suggested that you thought there was no preamble to adding a secondhand Chamber beyond coming across the Chamber, which was the source of my &quot;Well, no.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My fault for being unspecific, I took that as granted and should not have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003524#post1003524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>You specifically have to have been there to add the Chamber</b> and I was not suggesting knowledge of the inciting monster in the sense of acquaintance; you don't <i>need</i> to be friends with the vampire that formed a Chamber to incorporate it, but you do need to know how they caused a mortal to suffer a breaking point and how that vampire is distinguished from other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis Mine.<br /> <br /> Untrue, although unlikely, you could have come upon the Chamber within the Primordial Dream (having gotten into the Dream outside your Lair by unspecified means) and went through the research and Chamber adding process without ever having actually gone to the physical location the Chamber is based on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003524#post1003524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the context of &quot;you are consciously reaching for a random [location-type analogous to one of your Chambers],&quot; yes, you are not going to have the necessary knowledge of a random location to be able to angle for the ease of transport which comes from having a specific narrative associated with both you and your destination point.<br /> <br /> You're not going to be able to exploit the fact that somebody was tortured/was subject to a powerful Nightmare/encountered a monster in a <i>random location</i> through the fact that you're in a Chamber based on that kind of location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? I realize it would be unlikely and difficult, but what in the book actually prevents it from occurring?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:54:52-08:00","id":1003583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003561#post1003561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Untrue, although unlikely, you could have come upon the Chamber within the Primordial Dream (having gotten into the Dream outside your Lair by unspecified means) and went through the research and Chamber adding process without ever having actually gone to the physical location the Chamber is based on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am counting the Chamber and its seed as one location for the purposes of &quot;being there&quot; and the likelihood of accomplishing that research without ever encountering the material area is absurdly low in light of how physical navigation is less constrained than the Pathways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not? I realize it would be unlikely and difficult, but what in the book actually prevents it from occurring? </div> </div> </div>The fact that it is a random location and declaring a specific degree of connection to your Legend that is not intrinsic to the physical nature of the location is at odds with the idea that you are simply angling for any location analogous to one of your Chambers.<br /> <br /> The point of Chamber resonance is to encourage players to use the things that formed their Chambers as the template for building up a pattern that they can exploit to move across their extended hunting grounds easily. It's a territory-expansion mechanism.<br /> <br /> A character isn't going to blindly reach through the Dream to get to a place they've never been via a hazy connection they have no established awareness of; they're pushing through to <i>a [Chamber type]</i> in [realm] on the basis of there being any [Chamber type] in [realm] at all, and a connection based solely on [Chamber type] is descriptive similarity regardless of whether something went down to form a Chamber in a place they pulled out of a hat through means they have no foreknowledge of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:12:28-08:00","id":1003595,"title":"","content":"Alright, new argument: Forcing the penalty for a random jump to always be -5 means the penalty is effectively -8 <i>all the time. </i>That's too fucking big for a single penalty, which under your interpretation it basically is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:23:09-08:00","id":1003605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003595#post1003595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, new argument: Forcing the penalty for a random jump to always be -5 means the penalty is effectively -8 <i>all the time. </i>That's too fucking big for a single penalty, which under your interpretation it basically is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost as though this makes random jumps better suited to Beasts who are Gorged and/or powerful and/or in a brood moving to places outside the material realm that have a lot of Lair Traits in common, yes.<br /> <br /> This is an Attribute-based pool and the penalty for going to a random location goes away for each specific location you successfully reach regardless of how well it's integrated into your Legend and one of the components of the roll is essentially the most strongly incentivized Attribute for you to raise as a Beast. The Lair does not function especially well as a launching platform for ventures into other dimensions unless you put the work in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:49:42-08:00","id":1003647,"title":"","content":"No, when I say it's too big for a single penalty I mean <i>it's too big, and therefore cannot be a single penalty. </i>If your interpretation was the one intended then the penalty for a random jump just flat-out <i>isn't -3. </i>Therefore the fact that it was <i>given </i>as -3 means that you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-15-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:50:48-08:00","id":1003674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003647#post1003647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, when I say it's too big for a single penalty I mean <i>it's too big, and therefore cannot be a single penalty. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>And lo and behold, it is in fact two penalties, one of which inherently goes away on subsequent visits to that same location through the Pathways.<br /> <br /> Getting out of the Lair and into another location only requires a single success on the Pathway roll and using that roll as your means of getting to a place without associating yourself with it first is substantially penalized even if you aim for a specific location.<br /> <br /> Mage similarly hypothetically trucks with double-digit penalties that <i>are</i> explicitly larger than five dice individually, can be offset by bonuses, and only need a single rolled success to work, and I've yet to see claims that this is a flaw with the mechanics of Awakened magic despite the largest that pool's baseline gets being fifteen dice without a character opting to break into the secret heart of the universe and shoot for godhood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your interpretation was the one intended then the penalty for a random jump just flat-out <i>isn't -3. </i>Therefore the fact that it was <i>given </i>as -3 means that you're wrong. </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's -8 dice to jump from your forest Chamber to a forest in the material world that you haven't hunted in and haven't got a Lair Trait for if you know where it is you're going, rising to -11 dice if you have absolutely no idea where it is you're going besides 'a forest in the material world that has no ties to my Legend and none of my Lair Traits.'&quot;<br /> <br /> The penalty for a random jump exists alongside the suite of penalties for using a similar location to one of your Chambers to open a Pathway and only lasts as long as it takes for you to roll a single success. Where does a problem exist with discouraging the use of random jaunts without substantial power or preparation in this gameline where your territory is a part of you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:05:20-08:00","id":1003686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003674#post1003674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It's -8 dice to jump from your forest Chamber to a forest in the material world that you haven't hunted in and haven't got a Lair Trait for if you know where it is you're going, rising to -11 dice if you have absolutely no idea where it is you're going besides 'a forest in the material world that has no ties to my Legend and none of my Lair Traits.'&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except THAT'S NOT WHAT YOU'RE DOING.You're feeling around the reality for a weak point to push through into. IE somewhere <i>with</i> your lair traits, and <i>with </i>some narrative resonance to the chamber you're in.<br /> <br /> IT SHOULDN'T BE HARDER, BECAUSE YOU'RE TRADING ACCURACY FOR EASE OF PASSAGE. THAT IS THE ENTIRE FUCKING POINT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-15-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:28:52-08:00","id":1003697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003686#post1003686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except THAT'S NOT WHAT YOU'RE DOING.You're feeling around the reality for a weak point to push through into. IE somewhere <i>with</i> your lair traits, and <i>with </i>some narrative resonance to the chamber you're in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lair Traits are a semiconsistent function of a location's similarity to one of your Chambers \u2014 the presence or absence of a Trait is not a function of unknown history \u2014 but the degrees of resonance between perfect recreation and mere conceptual similarity engage with the Beast's connection to an event that expanded the Primordial Dream \u2014 a connection that is not impersonal and nonspecific enough to justify the claim that activities without even a secondary tie to the Beast could be deliberately pursued as a random pull.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IT SHOULDN'T BE HARDER, BECAUSE YOU'RE TRADING ACCURACY FOR EASE OF PASSAGE. THAT IS THE ENTIRE FUCKING POINT. </div> </div> </div>This is an ability you have by virtue of the habitual and territorial idmonster you have where humans have a soul. Why should the power of the Horror more readily flow to a literally random point in a specified world than it would a place that's just similar in type of location but still possessed of some familiarity to you?<br /> <br /> And that <i>is</i> what you're proposing by saying that the random-destination penalty takes the place of the penalty for resonance \u2014 that a legendary monster whose range is a function of the repetition of its territorial claims and has its life bound to that of the human who directs its activities while conscious and focused is somehow <i>more</i> inclined to leap to a random lightless hovel in the Underworld than it is to reach out and merge with a Beast who just entered that same lightless hovel.<br /> <br /> Wherefore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:46:12-08:00","id":1003709,"title":"","content":"The odds of hitting a particular thing you're aiming at are always smaller than the odds of hitting <i>something</i> when you don't aim at all. How are you not grasping this concept?<br /> <br /> The horror <i>isn't </i>more likely to appear in a random hovel than merge with a beast calling it there. It's more likely to emerge at <i>a</i> random hovel than merge with a beast calling it at <i>that specific one. </i>The odds of it appearing in any <i>particular</i> area are quite small.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-15-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:09:09-08:00","id":1003718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003709#post1003709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odds of hitting a particular thing you're aiming at are always smaller than the odds of hitting <i>something</i> when you don't aim at all. How are you not grasping this concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because opening a Pathway is not inherently an in-universe roll of the dice, all the ways invoking the Lair works otherwise key off of the patterns of behavior and similarity in which the power of the Beast, Horror, and Lair are concentrated, and nothing about the game as written suggests Beasts winding up oceans away from home and stranded until they can establish a proper connection to their territory is a common occurrence.<br /> <br /> Everything about the way resonance works suggests that you are in fact aiming in general \u2014 the Pathways connect a cave Chamber to any caves in theory, but caves which are dark and flooded connect more readily to the cave Chamber of a Beast whose Lair resonates with those qualities that you can feel by being exposed to them. A random pull is wandering into a new location, not shining a flashlight at the wall and saying &quot;That way.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The horror <i>isn't </i>more likely to appear in a random hovel than merge with a beast calling it there. It's more likely to emerge at <i>a</i> random hovel than merge with a beast calling it at <i>that specific one. </i> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Pathways connecting a Beast's Lair to the outside world don't distinguish between these two activities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The odds of it appearing in any <i>particular</i> area are quite small. </div> </div> </div>If opening a Pathway in general worked by throwing darts at the map, sure, but Pathways aren't darts, least of all when their primary function is to connect you to yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:15:39-08:00","id":1003721,"title":"","content":"Darts is the wrong analogy here. It's more like throwing yourself at a wall and seeing which bit gives. And since you have to be <i>in </i>your lair to do a random jump &quot;connecting to yourself&quot; has nothing to do with it. <br /> <br /> Why would you even <i>do</i> a random jump if it was harder? There's no benefit at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:52:36-08:00","id":1003753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003721#post1003721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darts is the wrong analogy here. It's more like throwing yourself at a wall and seeing which bit gives. And since you have to be <i>in </i>your lair to do a random jump &quot;connecting to yourself&quot; has nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Pathway is a Pathway whether you're in your Lair or out of it and the Pathways you make from out of it most unambiguously connect your Horror's location in the Lair to your own location in the wider world and merge you with the monster.<br /> <br /> You're arguing for random jumps using the Pathways to arbitrarily work <i>completely differently</i> from how every other use of Primordial Pathways within the same mechanic does despite every other aspect of this corner of Begotten metaphysics working against the idea that unplanned decisions not filtered through your history are somehow more likely to bear fruit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would you even <i>do</i> a random jump if it was harder? There's no benefit at all. </div> </div> </div>There's no benefit at all to doing a random jump in the first place regardless, so I'm rather lost as to why it's so important that it be easier to do.<br /> <br /> Like, there's a case to be made for the penalties for Chamber resonance only applying to exterior entry rolls and having the random jaunt penalty sub in for those in interior exit rolls \u2014 the scaling odds of multiple successes are largely irrelevant in exit rolls when you instantly separate from the Horror. \u2014 but by pushing for the possibility that the intermediate degrees of resonance have a real chance of deliberate invocation in the nonspecific target option you've effectively been arguing that either:<br /> <br /> 1) You can somehow have the Horror sort potential exits by history when you have to manually do the legwork for that even with chunks of the Primordial Dream you are literally touching.<br /> <br /> Or:<br /> <br /> 2) The thing that relies on you being alive to eat and live is going to be more comfortable tossing you across the cosmos than sending you someplace you've been to that is like the place it already occupies.<br /> <br /> My position is that &quot;random destination in specified realm&quot; is an extra penalty that applies to using descriptive similarity to access an unknown location for the first time, because casual long-distance teleportation is something I read Beast's metaphysics as making uncommon and prep-work-intensive. Where are you getting the idea that easy random jumps are better from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-15-2016, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T22:27:33-08:00","id":1003783,"title":"","content":"It'd really be great the get the writer for these sections in here to clarify things. It's all so poorly organized that I'm still not 100% convinced that we didn't get two halves of two different systems from two different stages of development that work completely differently from each other.<br /> <br /> It's so backwards to present a table of reasonable penalties in the section describing an action, and then present another table of completely different, still reasonable penalties for the same action in a completely different area, after the book as moved on to a new topic Especially when, combined, the penalties begin to seem less reasonable (although I agree with your interpretation that they are meant to stack, Satchel).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T22:29:38-08:00","id":1003785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003686#post1003686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IT SHOULDN'T BE HARDER, BECAUSE YOU'RE TRADING ACCURACY FOR EASE OF PASSAGE. THAT IS THE ENTIRE FUCKING POINT.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Dude, chill.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:32:32-08:00","id":1003821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003785#post1003785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Dude, chill.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry about that. I shouldn't let myself get into arguments at 1am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-16-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:34:03-08:00","id":1003955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003709#post1003709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odds of hitting a particular thing you're aiming at are always smaller than the odds of hitting <i>something</i> when you don't aim at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at it this way: If you want to punch through a wall you really want to do it where you know the wall is weaker. Just randomly throwing a punch at the wall will require more oomph behind the punch than if you've already located a weak spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:43:42-08:00","id":1003957,"title":"","content":"You haven't located a weak spot though. You've located the spot you happen to want to punch though. When you just spread out and probe for a random location you're going to get places with lair traits and good resonances.<br /> <br /> So even if you add the location penalty, it should <i>never </i>be -5. That would mean that given the choice of <i>any possible location</i> your horror automatically gravitates to the <i>least </i>suitable one it can use at all, which is patently absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:55:21-08:00","id":1003963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003583#post1003583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am counting the Chamber and its seed as one location for the purposes of &quot;being there&quot; and the likelihood of accomplishing that research without ever encountering the material area is absurdly low in light of how physical navigation is less constrained than the Pathways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough on the first point. I was really only questioning the absoluteness of your previous statements; here you say that it is absurdly low but not impossible, and that's fine by me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003583#post1003583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that it is a random location and declaring a specific degree of connection to your Legend that is not intrinsic to the physical nature of the location is at odds with the idea that you are simply angling for any location analogous to one of your Chambers.<br /> <br /> The point of Chamber resonance is to encourage players to use the things that formed their Chambers as the template for building up a pattern that they can exploit to move across their extended hunting grounds easily. It's a territory-expansion mechanism.<br /> <br /> A character isn't going to blindly reach through the Dream to get to a place they've never been via a hazy connection they have no established awareness of; they're pushing through to <i>a [Chamber type]</i> in [realm] on the basis of there being any [Chamber type] in [realm] at all, and a connection based solely on [Chamber type] is descriptive similarity regardless of whether something went down to form a Chamber in a place they pulled out of a hat through means they have no foreknowledge of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't assuming that the character was declaring a specific degree or anything like that. Only that the players (including the Storyteller) might decide that such a location is what is found and that increases the likelyhood of the successful random jump. This has the benefit of allowing the Storyteller to lead the character where they want them to go with an in-universe justification and also provides the player with a new known location that they can then use in the future. Purely an out of character narrative device that I wanted to justify within the metaphysics of the setting. I think we are on the same page here.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:12:47-08:00","id":1004049,"title":"","content":"Sparing myself a headache as well as getting people to get back to ground:<br /> <br /> What are we arguing about here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:51:58-08:00","id":1004068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004049#post1004049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sparing myself a headache as well as getting people to get back to ground:<br /> <br /> What are we arguing about here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I see it, there have been three (and a half) different points:<br /> <br /> 1) A clarification request on the penalties for opening a Primordial Pathway, with a suggestion that they were too harsh if read the way they seemed to.<br /> 1.5) Some discussion on the organization/editing of the book that may have contributed to the confusion in the first point.<br /> 2) Elfive and Satchel began discussing the metaphysical and mechanical nature of opening a Pathway blindly.<br /> 3) I jumped in to ask questions of Satch's interpretation and attempt to clarify what I thought Elfive's position was. Elfive and my conversations with Satchel diverged enough for me to list them here separately. I also believe that Satchel and my's discussion has run its course (unless Satchel would like to add anything).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> , please feel free to correct me if I am wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  fixed spelling 11-16-2016, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:30:13-08:00","id":1004220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004068#post1004068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Elfive and Satchel began discussing the metaphysical and mechanical nature of opening a Pathway blindly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> , please feel free to correct me if I am wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>A prominent subclause of the second point is whether any degree of Chamber resonance greater than descriptive similarity can meaningfully apply to blindly opening a Pathway, but yes, that's about the size of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1003957#post1003957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't located a weak spot though. You've located the spot you happen to want to punch though. When you just spread out and probe for a random location you're going to get places with lair traits and good resonances.</div> </div> </div> </div>And good resonances by default key off of things that are connected to your personal Legend and your place in it, which, again, doesn't mesh with a random push the way narrowing your search to &quot;someplace burning&quot; or &quot;somewhere swarming with bugs&quot; does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So even if you add the location penalty, it should <i>never </i>be -5. That would mean that given the choice of <i>any possible location</i> your horror automatically gravitates to the <i>least </i>suitable one it can use at all, which is patently absurd. </div> </div> </div>Because, again, the least suitable one it can use at all is the one you are consciously directing the power of your Lair toward on account of that being the only degree of connection to a random location that you can rely upon.<br /> <br /> Secondhand Chambers have an explicit shelf life beyond the immediate formation chance and get incorporated through your essentially consuming the story of what went down in a given location, but Beasts don't have an inherent bond with clandestine killer psyche-fractures the way they do, say, slashers \u2014 treating the hazy in-absentia echoing of a breaking point roll you were once present for the same as such a repetition where you're actually in the area means that you have to assume the Begotten have a sense for not just the seeds of Chambers but the near-miss opportunities for Chambers to have formed, and that's a degree of awareness that would merit at least as much attention as Family Resemblance just for the sheer quantity of data such a sense would make available.<br /> <br /> So if the resonance penalty persists on a random jump \u2014 and I feel I've made my case for it doing so unless you actually have an argument for <i>why</i> random jumps being more likely to succeed than a jump to a known location with a weak connection is a desirable mechanical and thematic outcome \u2014 then it uses the only degree of similarity you can rely upon, because narrative and spiritual similarity call for your presence or at least your knowledge on the basis that Beasts do not have a natural sense for events that replicate the roots of their Chambers that would logically be discernible just by trying to open Pathways from random analogues. You had to be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-16-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T01:53:49-08:00","id":1004296,"title":"","content":"What the FUCK does second-hand chamber's shelf life even have to do with this? You don't <i>need </i>a chamber to form in an area to use it to access your lair, and even if you did, the resonant event needs to be happening <i>right now. </i>The fact that the chamber potentially formed (which it wouldn't even be, if we're talking narrative-tier) isn't going to last very long is irrelevant. It last's long enough for us.<br /> <br /> You are assuming that I'm assuming things that I am <i>very much not assuming. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T09:19:28-08:00","id":1004465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004296#post1004296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the FUCK does second-hand chamber's shelf life even have to do with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally the only example presented of Beasts having even a dim awareness of the history of a location without having been there, which is the sort of thing you'd need to know to be able to deliberately access a location through resonance you couldn't possibly guess at instead of the resonance of &quot;it's a gas station.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't <i>need </i>a chamber to form in an area to use it to access your lair, and even if you did, the resonant event needs to be happening <i>right now. </i> </div> </div> </div>There is no actually-presented evidence that resonance beyond exact similarity has an expiration date and in fact assuming the resonance only applies in the moment does very little to support the idea that Beasts use their Legends to expand their territory \u2014 the only reason to try to enhance the resonance of a location would then be to invoke Lair Traits without a base Tilt or to pull someone into the Lair then and there, and if you're doing the latter to a mortal they're suffering a breaking point anyway and probably don't need to be face to face with your Horror to suffer from the presence of your Traits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that the chamber potentially formed (which it wouldn't even be, if we're talking narrative-tier) isn't going to last very long is irrelevant. It last's long enough for us. </div> </div> </div>My interpretation of the intermediate resonance levels is that they last basically indefinitely by default regardless of whether the area links to a Chamber, which is precisely why I've been arguing against their applicability to random pushes based on unknowable knowledge of a place's history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are assuming that I'm assuming things that I am <i>very much not assuming. </i> </div> </div> </div>Your presented actual assumptions here are getting further off the map, which is very definitely not something I have any control over.<br /> <br /> 1. Why, the urgency of the descriptive similarity example notwithstanding, should greater resonance only last long enough to invoke the Lair right then and there when the Begotten, the Primordial Dream, and much of the supernatural in general key off of the tone and history of things and places and the two more esoteric means of accessing the Pathways both have no expiration date short of &quot;the access vector is destroyed&quot;?<br /> <br /> 2. Why should the Begotten be able to use narrative similarity to places with no connection to them or the supernatural beings whose handiwork they've internalized when they have no presented ability to innately discern that such a narrative is playing out even just outside the grasp of their senses and the ability to use a lesser penalty for following the resonance of a new location would de facto give them at least a vague sense of information akin to something they need to be physically present for and engage in active investigation to uncover to more directly link a place to the Lair?<br /> <br /> 3. Why should using a connection between places you are associated with directly or by proxy to change your location be any easier to do to a random place you've never visited than via the weakest possible connection you have to a place you've been before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T09:38:02-08:00","id":1004479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004465#post1004465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. Why should using a connection between places you are associated with directly or by proxy to change your location be any easier to do to a random place you've never visited than via the weakest possible connection you have to a place you've been before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're not doing it to <i>a</i> random place, you're doing it to <i>literally every random place on the planet simultaneously, including places you HAVE already been. </i>If your target destination is &quot;anywhere but here&quot; then <i>of course</i> you're more likely to get somewhere. You're taking all the effort at pinpointing a destination and pushing it into just getting out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:08:00-08:00","id":1004499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004479#post1004479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you're not doing it to <i>a</i> random place, you're doing it to <i>literally every random place on the planet simultaneously, including places you HAVE already been. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're doing it to any random [location type] in a given world, picked at random. Spinning the globe and putting your finger on it is not smashing your fist through the thing. If you want to go to a place that you've already been, you angle for a Pathway to the place that you've already been.<br /> <br /> You're looking for an abandoned warehouse that the East Side Pyro could conceivably be in based on the fact that the East Side Pyro is a Beast who has associated their Primordial Self with an abandoned warehouse through Nightmares or Kinship or breaking points, and the nature of most abandoned warehouses is to be related to the East Side Pyro solely through that connection, particularly when the East Side Pyro has never been to those abandoned warehouses.<br /> <br /> You're pointing a finger, not firing a shotgun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your target destination is &quot;anywhere but here&quot; then <i>of course</i> you're more likely to get somewhere. </div> </div> </div>And why, exactly, is &quot;anywhere but here&quot; the sort of destination that <i>should</i> be easy to get to by basically any Beast at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're taking all the effort at pinpointing a destination and pushing it into just getting out. </div> </div> </div>And again, given that you are doing this from the place where a monster whose death is synonymous with your death exists and &quot;effort at pinpointing a destination&quot; is the opposite of what greater resonance represents when opening a Pathway normally, why should this be a valid mechanical/thematic outcome?<br /> <br /> There's no emergency utility to making a random jump thanks to the way Health works when you're merged, so thusfar your argument has almost entirely hinged on the vague supposition that it &quot;should&quot; work this way because of reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:32:45-08:00","id":1004511,"title":"","content":"If you recall, my original argument was that you shouldn't apply a penalty based on the destination similarity because <i>you don't know what that is.</i> My secondary argument was that assuming that it's as low as possible is counter-intuitive, because why would <i>that </i> be the place you managed to force your way through into? It should have any one of a number of features that lower the penalty by an unspecified amount. <br /> <br /> So, my final conclusion, which I may have not made clear, was that, rather than the -3 being an <i>additional</i> penalty, it was simply an <i>average</i> of the preexisting penalties summed over the whole realm.<br /> <br /> In the last four pages you have done nothing to dissuade me of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:54:10-08:00","id":1004790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004511#post1004511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you recall, my original argument was that you shouldn't apply a penalty based on the destination similarity because <i>you don't know what that is.</i> My secondary argument was that assuming that it's as low as possible is counter-intuitive, because why would <i>that </i> be the place you managed to force your way through into?</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of locations whose type matches one of your Chambers are going to have nothing to do with you by the mere fact that you have not been to most of the caves, forests, shacks, lakes, etc in <i>the material world</i>, never mind your pick of a handful of realms less innately connected to you than the Dreams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It should have any one of a number of features that lower the penalty by an unspecified amount. </div> </div> </div>That would be the goal of including the bonus for Lair Traits in the roll to begin with, which are separate from the resonance penalty in the first place and only tangentially related to the matter of whether things somehow match things personally relevant to the way you acquired a Chamber.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, my final conclusion, which I may have not made clear, was that, rather than the -3 being an <i>additional</i> penalty, it was simply an <i>average</i> of the preexisting penalties summed over the whole realm. </div> </div> </div>The rounded median of the existing penalties as a list is a substantially better chance of success than the rounded median of the vast majority of randomly chosen basements, attics, wells, construction yards, etc in the world, which is by no means clearly the way that process is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the last four pages you have done nothing to dissuade me of this. </div> </div> </div>And I've now asked you the same question three times consecutively and you have dodged it on each occasion:<br /> <br /> <i>Why, mechanically and thematically, should a random jump be easier to succeed at than a long-shot stretch to a known destination? What gives you cause to believe that this is the intended reading of the mechanic, other than a broad conviction that that's the way it ought to work?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T23:53:08-08:00","id":1004820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004790#post1004790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I've now asked you the same question three times consecutively and you have dodged it on each occasion:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>NO<br /> <br /> I<br /> <br /> FUCKING<br /> <br /> HAVEN'T<br /> <br /> YOU JUST KEEP DISMISSING MY ANSWER.<br /> <br /> You did it here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would be the goal of including the bonus for Lair Traits in the roll to begin with, which are separate from the resonance penalty in the first place and only tangentially related to the matter of whether things somehow match things personally relevant to the way you acquired a Chamber. </div> </div> </div>Resonance and lair trait bonuses are not &quot;tangentially related&quot; because they <i>directly cancel each other out.</i> They are <i>intricately </i>linked and in a blind jump you know <i>neither </i>(because <i>you </i>haven't explained why,say, if you're in a chamber formed by someone who lost integrity to lunacy how that's not at least <i>narratively</i> similar to someone <i>else</i> losing integrity to lunacy at a similar location) and so you're left trying to assign a penalty that's utterly random.<br /> <br /> It just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Also you don't actually have to have <i>been</i> to a place you're aiming at. There's no penalty assigned to that. So your repeated assertion that a random location should be harder because you don't have a connection to it is fallacious too.<br /> <br /> In fact, <i>all</i> your arguments for this strike me as overly-restrictive interpretation of the requirements for two places to connect. The Primordial Dream is <i>everywhere. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-18-2016, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T00:22:09-08:00","id":1004826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004820#post1004820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YOU JUST KEEP DISMISSING MY ANSWER.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have asked, multiple times, why a random jump <i>should</i> be easier to do than a jump, from a mechanical and thematic standpoint as far as what gives you cause to think the mechanic is supposed to work that way.<br /> <br /> You have given several answers to the question of what you suppose the metaphysical/metaphorical justification for that reading working that way is, but I still have nothing to go off of for why you think that a random jump <i>is supposed to be</i> comparatively easy, because you <i>keep avoiding that part of the question.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resonance and lair trait bonuses are not &quot;tangentially related&quot; because they <i>directly cancel each other out.</i> </div> </div> </div>Yes, by <i>being bonuses and penalties</i>. &quot;Random jumps include nebulous factors that somehow total to a net penalty between 'something happened that was a near-miss to forming a Chamber in your Lair here' and 'something happened that would have formed a Chamber in your Lair here if you felt the need to use such a limited space on adding a conceptual duplicate of one of your Chambers to your list of Chambers' despite the overwhelming majority of locations matching the baseline description of one of your Chambers not having even the weaker of those two degrees of connection, and this mitigation exists independently of and stacks with the bonus Lair Traits provide&quot; is by no means an intuitive reading of the Pathway mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are <i>intricately </i>linked and in a blind jump you know <i>neither </i>(because <i>you </i>haven't explained why,say, if you're in a chamber formed by someone who lost integrity to lunacy how that's not at least <i>narratively</i> similar to someone <i>else</i> losing integrity to lunacy at a similar location) and so you're left trying to assign a penalty that's utterly random. </div> </div> </div>I've explained it multiple times: <i>You are a specific Beast trying to use your connection to things related to you as a specific Beast to go to places tied to you as a specific Beast on the basis of those locations being where you have been and therefore can be.</i><br /> <br /> If you're in a Chamber formed by someone losing Integrity to Lunacy, opening a Pathway based on narrative similarity keys off of the fact that you are a Beast who has been present for someone with a connection to you or a werewolf whose handiwork you have taken inspiration from losing Integrity to Lunacy in a context that is assuredly not as nonspecific as &quot;someone lost Integrity to Lunacy.&quot; A Primal Urge 8 elder wolf breaking someone's mind by assuming Gauru in front of a small group paints a different picture than a Shape-Shifted Wolf-Blood scaring the living daylights out of a lone hiker, and having been present for one event in no way implies connection to the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also you don't actually have to have <i>been</i> to a place you're aiming at. There's no penalty assigned to that. </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is. That's one of the reasons to actually bother with resonance based solely on descriptive similarity besides a time crunch. You wanna use your pine forest Chamber to jump to a pine forest in Saskatchewan? Do some research and find out some stuff about a pine forest in Saskatchewan, maybe make some calls to get some on-the-ground photos and add some of your Lair Traits to the place, and embark.<br /> <br /> That's how aiming <i>works</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-18-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T00:50:08-08:00","id":1004832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004826#post1004826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have given several answers to the question of what you suppose the metaphysical/metaphorical justification for that reading working that way is, but I still have nothing to go off of for why you think that a random jump <i>is supposed to be</i> comparatively easy, because you <i>keep avoiding that part of the question.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's an inherent trade-off in the fact that you don't get to pick where you go. That requires compensation of some sort, which to me suggests that it should be easier for some reason, of which I have already given plenty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T01:13:50-08:00","id":1004836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004832#post1004832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there's an inherent trade-off in the fact that you don't get to pick where you go. That requires compensation of some sort, which to me suggests that it should be easier for some reason, of which I have already given plenty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I view &quot;you can utterly disrupt the narrative and bend the story around to the pursuit of Lair-expansion in a faraway and possibly foreign location&quot; as the kind of last-resort no-better-ideas option that is theoretically possible for characters bound to perennial terrors to make use of but absolutely not something you want sitting around as a viable story-rerouter right from the early stages of a chronicle.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a bigger penalty, so there must be a compensation for doing this thing that is most useful to powerful characters who've hit a stumbling block and don't need to worry as much about the consequences of intruding upon the domains of gods or being in a place where you don't speak the language and your network coverage doesn't apply and half your electronics don't have the right plugs for the wall outlets&quot; doesn't seem terribly thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T02:10:40-08:00","id":1004843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004820#post1004820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NO<br /> <br /> I<br /> <br /> FUCKING<br /> <br /> HAVEN'T<br /> <br /> YOU JUST KEEP DISMISSING MY ANSWER.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You need to tone down the aggressive responses. Please don't make me have to address the issue again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T05:37:08-08:00","id":1004893,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think I need to just ignore this topic and not post in it from now on. It's clearly getting to me. I'm not normally like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:09:51-08:00","id":1004900,"title":"","content":"Page 97 under Primordial Pathways states &quot;If a Beast doesn't know exactly where she wants to go, she can feel for and open a Pathway to somewhere random but still resonant within a specified world.&quot; There is a chart of suggested modifiers associated with that specific section, which would most likely stack. So a Beast leaving their Lair to a random location in the material world would end up somewhere that is resonant with their Lair if they succeeded with a -3 for material, -3 for imprecise location, and any positive modifiers the ST decided to grant for having any relevant Lair traits in the location.<br /> <br /> At worst, it looks like you'd have -6 for the dice roll to go anywhere in the material world that is resonant to your Lair that's random, or -3 for the dice roll to anywhere in the material world that is resonant to your Lair that you know of. I figure a Beast would have a solid idea of what's resonant to their Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:41:07-08:00","id":1004909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004900#post1004900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At worst, it looks like you'd have -6 for the dice roll to go anywhere in the material world that is resonant to your Lair that's random, or -3 for the dice roll to anywhere in the material world that is resonant to your Lair that you know of. I figure a Beast would have a solid idea of what's resonant to their Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd think so, but then in the section about Lair traits they list additional penalties to opening pathways that range from -2 to -5 (that apparently stack with the ones in that section). So the actual penalty to go anywhere in the material world that's resonant is -5 at minimum, to -11 for a random location with descriptive similarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:43:57-08:00","id":1005023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1004909#post1004909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd think so, but then in the section about Lair traits they list additional penalties to opening pathways that range from -2 to -5 (that apparently stack with the ones in that section). So the actual penalty to go anywhere in the material world that's resonant is -5 at minimum, to -11 for a random location with descriptive similarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about the section titled &quot;Chambers and Lair Traits&quot; on page 101?<br /> <br /> That's specifically directed to a Beast's ability to inflict his Lair Traits on his current location. The factors of &quot;Exact&quot;, &quot;Spiritual Similarity&quot;, &quot;Narrative Similarity&quot; and &quot;Descriptive Similarity&quot; only matter when you're trying to alter the environment with your Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> I can see that the descriptions of those four do make mention of Opening Primordial Pathways. However, the actual section that covers the rules of Opening Primordial Pathways makes absolutely no reference to this criteria. It makes more sense to me to think the mention of further restriction on Primordial Pathways in a section that is for an entirely different topic and does not start out describing the process of opening Primordial Pathways is an artifact of the text having been altered at some point and this reference is in error. <br /> <br /> If opening Primordial Pathways was restricted by similarity to this extent, then the section dedicated to the mechanics of it should have referenced or made previous mention of it. In effect, allowing the interpretation that a section on invoking Lair Traits as being prescriptive of altering the rules of Opening Primordial Pathways has a &quot;double dipping&quot; effect of penalties. <br /> <br /> Even more telling is that there's no consideration as to what your Heart Chamber would function as under these levels, as that Chamber doesn't have a material world correspondence and therefore cannot qualify under &quot;Exact&quot;. <br /> <br /> So the Chamber and Lair Traits section has to be in error, because it's talking about the wrong section for those details, does not get references by the actual section for those details and it doesn't make sense to penalize a player twice for the same quality. <br /> <br /> If you like the more specific consideration of similarity of your environment, I recommend dropping the -3 penalty described under Opening Primordial Pathways for a material location unrelated to your Chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:03:59-08:00","id":1005094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005023#post1005023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you talking about the section titled &quot;Chambers and Lair Traits&quot; on page 101?<br /> <br /> That's specifically directed to a Beast's ability to inflict his Lair Traits on his current location. The factors of &quot;Exact&quot;, &quot;Spiritual Similarity&quot;, &quot;Narrative Similarity&quot; and &quot;Descriptive Similarity&quot; only matter when you're trying to alter the environment with your Lair Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wish it was that straightforward. This entire thread has been about the fact that no, it isn't.<br /> <br /> That's kind of why I pointed out in the OP, and further in the thread, that the editing of the Lair section has absolutely destroyed any kind of cohesiveness and made the intention of the penalties incredibly unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:50:50-08:00","id":1005115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005094#post1005094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish it was that straightforward. This entire thread has been about the fact that no, it isn't.<br /> <br /> That's kind of why I pointed out in the OP, and further in the thread, that the editing of the Lair section has absolutely destroyed any kind of cohesiveness and made the intention of the penalties incredibly unclear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. My thinking here is... These books are not perfect. Mistakes can and will make it past editing. That's a simple reality to acknowledge. What this means is that a critical reading will identify support for the text through context in order to have a better idea of what the intended interpretation is (note, in saying &quot;idea&quot;, I can't know for sure). <br /> <br /> What this means, is that the text simply existing does not in itself justify its correctness. Further support is necessary. <br /> <br /> So, my question to you is: &quot;What supports your interpretation of a section that does not involve the subject of opening Primordial Pathways, to have valid rules for the subject of opening Primordial Pathways, when those rules are not mentioned at all in the specified section that addresses that very subject matter?&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you have any further reasoning beyond &quot;Its written there&quot;? Why do you think it might not just be an editing error, wouldn't that be the simplest explanation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:52:08-08:00","id":1005119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005115#post1005115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. My thinking here is... These books are not perfect. Mistakes can and will make it past editing. That's a simple reality to acknowledge. What this means is that a critical reading will identify support for the text through context in order to have a better idea of what the intended interpretation is (note, in saying &quot;idea&quot;, I can't know for sure).<br /> <br /> What this means, is that the text simply existing does not in itself justify its correctness. Further support is necessary.<br /> <br /> So, my question to you is: &quot;What supports your interpretation of a section that does not involve the subject of opening Primordial Pathways, to have valid rules for the subject of opening Primordial Pathways, when those rules are not mentioned at all in the specified section that addresses that very subject matter?&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you have any further reasoning beyond &quot;Its written there&quot;? Why do you think it might not just be an editing error, wouldn't that be the simplest explanation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you actually read the thread? Satchel has spent pages going into a very valid explanation. I personally am house-ruling it to perfectly align with your interpretation, but the text (and a logical analysis) supports his.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T16:45:28-08:00","id":1005153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005119#post1005119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you actually read the thread? Satchel has spent pages going into a very valid explanation. I personally am house-ruling it to perfectly align with your interpretation, but the text (and a logical analysis) supports his.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, and best I'm able to determine, post #29 is their argument.<br /> <br /> I don't really find it persuasive. I don't see the text supporting their position, nor the thematic or logical analysis of it. Let me make my case. <br /> <br /> Primordial Pathways are a really key power to Beasts. It's truthfully their most impressive capability. Their aptitude is so strong for opening these Pathways that the very definition of Primordial Pathway cites, &quot;The paths to access the Primordial Dream. Beasts can do it fairly easily, and can open them for other beings with Kinship.&quot; (Glossary). Page 91 starts off, &quot;As the Masters of the Primordial Pathways, Beasts enjoy a nearly unmatched freedom to wander the different planes of existence.&quot; On the same page, the power Skeleton Key states that its due to this instinctive connection to Primordial Pathways that they're able to force open other mystical gateways. Under the Bed allows a Beast to rip open a Primordial Pathway utilizing the nightmares of a mortal. <br /> <br /> What the section of opening Primordial Pathways states that is very important here, is that &quot;As with many aspects of their Lair, it's the resonance, or similarity, between the Lair and somewhere else that affords access.&quot; Its interesting that it's specifically referring to the Lair itself, and not specifically Chambers. Page 93 points out that Chambers are a defined &quot;setting&quot; of a Lair. It's Traits which are called out as actually defining what the Lairs resonance is. Traits of a Lair are not defined by Chambers at all (although they're good inspiration for such). So when the section Primordial Pathways states that a Beast who doesn't know where they want to go, they can feel around and open a Pathway to somewhere that is resonant to them, that's not referring to a similar Chamber, but a similar environment with their Lair Traits, because that is what defines the resonance of a Lair. <br /> <br /> The Primordial Pathway section states that its easiest for a Beast to open a Pathway at a physical location the one of their Chambers is based on. But says they can do without that, with &quot;an additional dice penalty&quot; (singular), along with spending a Willpower point. The willpower point is a real cost there. Further, there's only a single penalty in the list for a material world location that isn't based on a Chamber. -3 This is still affected by any bonus dice the Beast gets for having any applicable Lair Traits active in the area, whether natural or bled through from his Lair, and this fits because the bonus you get is based on how resonant the location is with your Lair, and its Lair Traits that define a Lair's resonance. <br /> <br /> Regarding the Chambers and Lair Traits section... Remember that Chambers are just &quot;setting&quot;, they're not resonance. What this section is pertaining to is how to place the resonance of your Lair into the location by calling on a Lair Traits. The more divergent from a Chamber to exemplify to build your resonance, the more difficult it is. Each of the given levels of similarity are in direct follow up with a stated mechanic, &quot;To impose Traits into a substitute location like this, the player must succeed a Wits + Resolve roll, with a dice penalty based on how dissimilar the location used is.&quot; Note that its only Exact which mentions that using the exact location for a Chamber does not incur a dice penalty to opening a Primordial Pathway. And this is true! You actually get a dice bonus for doing so! <br /> <br /> However, for the other three examples, even though each makes a statement of INTENT to open a Primordial Pathway, the citation of a dice penalty is alone as a separate sentence. That's because the dice penalty is explicitly for the above mechanic for rolling to impose a Trait. The Beasts in the three examples are looking to impose Traits in order to make opening a Primordial Pathway easier. <br /> <br /> Therefore, these two sections are separate and there is no editing error here (though perhaps not worded most clearly). This means that the worst penalty a Beast will likely encounter for opening a Primordial Pathway will be -6 from their Lair to a random location that opens in the material world, where the location will still be resonant with the Beast's Lair. <br /> <br /> This is a powerful ability, but time and time again the book hammers on that Beasts have an instinctual grasp of Primordial Pathways and that its their Forte to wander from plane to plane as they wish. This is perhaps their greatest strength. <br /> <br /> The book just provides zero support for Primordial Pathways to be something that Beasts find difficult. I've provided citations from the book to support my argument and I hope it's found persuasive. If you can see any flaws in my reasoning, or something from the book I've missed, please let me know. I would like to take it into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:48:23-08:00","id":1005217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005023#post1005023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's specifically directed to a Beast's ability to inflict his Lair Traits on his current location. The factors of &quot;Exact&quot;, &quot;Spiritual Similarity&quot;, &quot;Narrative Similarity&quot; and &quot;Descriptive Similarity&quot; only matter when you're trying to alter the environment with your Lair Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The example concerns opening a Primordial Pathway and the scaled penalties for resonance <i>are</i> directly mentioned in the second paragraph on Primordial Pathways \u2014 &quot;desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use similar locations by i<b>ncurring an extra penalty based on how well the location matches</b>.&quot; It's not a coincidence that the penalty for spiritual similarity is exactly undone by the bonus from Gorged. Beasts are collectively the masters of the Pathways, but each individual Begotten only presides over a single chunk of territory in that resonates with their Legend and the kind of world-spanning leaps enabled by random jumps are explicitly one of the things that's listed as a <i>story hook for what the Incarnate might bring to a game</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primordial Pathways are a really key power to Beasts. </div> </div> </div>They're key to the ability to access and invoke the Lair, but there is a world of difference between &quot;You are mechanically encouraged to repeat the activities that spawned one of your Chambers in similar locations to expand the range of areas in which you can easily invoke Lair Traits and merge with your Horror&quot; and &quot;Despite being the first new supernatural splat since Changeling to have no innate or trivially inexpensive linguistic workaround and despite having an entire suite of powers that work based on the reinforcement of your established legend, you can hypothetically jump to a completely foreign country and nearly strand yourself because for some reason having no idea what you're doing is more likely to get you somewhere than attempting to use the fact that you are innately connected to a basement to jump to the basement in a house you know of but have never visited.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that its only Exact which mentions that using the exact location for a Chamber does not incur a dice penalty to opening a Primordial Pathway. And this is true! You actually get a dice bonus for doing so! </div> </div> </div>This is disingenuous, given that the section you're talking about applies as much to highly faithful replicas as to the original location, immediately goes on to specify that some Beasts outright move manmade structures that they've used as Chambers elsewhere to make use of the ease of passage they present, and is the first and only item on the list to describe the penalty in more detail than &quot;a penalty.&quot;<br /> <br /> Elfive's bowed out, so now the same question apparently falls to you: What is the thematic purpose of allowing any given Beast to hop halfway across the world to a place they've almost certainly never been by sheer probability, given that Beasts are territorial legendary monsters and not Saboteur Unchained casting the widest possible net for Behind the Curtain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-18-2016, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T22:18:43-08:00","id":1005243,"title":"","content":"All the world's a stage, but let's not mistake the props for the story.<br /> <br /> The Horrors of Beasts are ancient trends of fear and security born into a face scarred into being from the confluence of a moment in a place, when those ancient trends takes on a particular manifestation in a moment-an seasoned actor taking on a new mask, if you will. The Chamber that forms the Heart sets the standards, it creates the mood, the atmosphere, defines the sort of characters that may be acted out, but the it's tenor of realization as presence that enters into form, that becomes the roc, the dragon, the griffin, the character who defines the role. There are certain roles you give to the Rock and certain roles you give to Sir Ian McKellan, and while there may be some points you consider both for, they are very different actors with different considerations. So think of the relationship from Family/Hunger, Horror, and Lair as being a collision between the two extreme-the Lair is born from specific contexts that the more archetypal forces of Family and Hunger form the character of the Horror.<br /> <br /> The addition of Chambers is something of a moment of actualization, a crosspoints of reaffirming the core dimensions of the Horror's main themes and the realization and acceptance of varations on that theme, On recognizing the wider, deeper, more nuanced complexities of the core essence that makes the primal attitudes of man kind relevant in this day and age.<br /> <br /> The Primordial Pathway, as a gaming tool, is not intended to be only be a quick transit tool-in fact, it's really more a tool of establishing the set for the story of your character. It's a way to step up from merely bring in in your lair traits in full, it's escalating-it's bringing the poor unfortunate soul into you lair, it's ensuring that you are where you are needed to be to keep kids from fucking way too young.<br /> <br /> Now, I know what you're thinking-&quot;but Arc, if the point is to ensure that the Beast is acting on a stage appropriate for it's own story, then shouldn't it be good and right that they have easy access to any stage that merits their presence?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, no. Because there's masks, and there's masks that are <i>just for you/the play, darling</i>.<br /> <br /> The thing about Chambers and Chamber analgoues(the latter being the basis for the argument) is that theoretically any place, even any Chamber, can form an archetypal(read empty) enough place to facilitate any sort of archetypal play. An wheat field can be a place for a Giant or a Leviathan, a Predator or a Collector, depending on how you want to play it. But Horrors aren't merely archetypal, being the child of a deep context <i>and </i>fresh face, ie, specific context, ie, the nature of their Heart. Any place is merely a mask anyone can wear, so devoid of detail that a Beast can't connect their Heart to it, and really evoke the performance needed. Moving beyond masks to stages, it's like trying to compare a blank stage to one that at least has some set design work done, or is hosted at a place that is haunted or cited for romance or something like that.<br /> <br /> As a TL;DR version, consider this-Beasts are powered by their Horror,s and Horrors are defined by their <i>doing</i> rather than their <i>being</i>. Having a place they fit matters, but having a place that is set for the story they tell is far more imporant. So having a place they know and have influence over the 'stage direction' of means that that place is more of who they are then someplace that is not.<br /> <br /> Now this is something of a moot point, considering most of that is focused on bringing Lair Traits into a place that doesn't have it rather than actually utilizing the Primordial Pathways, but from what I can tell, the most pertinent fact of here are the World Penalties, which includes metaphysical distance, the Lair Trait Bonuses, which ensures the stage is more and more set for the Beast, and the Imprecise Location penalty, which frankly is just sense-when any theater will do, an expert on the subject isn't going to bother helping you find the place to perform, so at that point it really is darts. The max is -6 from two -3, and it seems avoidable by just keeping your story on point.<br /> <br /> Another factor is to consider the idea of the Beast as a wanderer and explorer of the worlds, that they, in their primordial nature, are archetypally more inclined to wandering and journeying than merely &quot;jumping&quot; from place to place, to actually travel, to experience in awe. Dragons are always found at mountains, but they still fly too and fro. The point of Lair is for <i>your mountain</i> to always be realtively close-but you still need to fly from place to place, and not <i>every</i> mountain is yours-some belong to the dwarves, until you take it.<br /> <br /> But the point is this-while a transport tool, and a damn cool one, the Primordial Pathways (and Imposing Lair traits roll) is really more of a way of evoking the narrative of your character and their Horror, and it plays out to the purpose of keeping your narrative, and Beast's broader narratives, on track","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T23:33:25-08:00","id":1005255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005217#post1005217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The example concerns opening a Primordial Pathway and the scaled penalties for resonance <i>are</i> directly mentioned in the second paragraph on Primordial Pathways \u2014 &quot;desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use similar locations by i<b>ncurring an extra penalty based on how well the location matches</b>.&quot; It's not a coincidence that the penalty for spiritual similarity is exactly undone by the bonus from Gorged. Beasts are collectively the masters of the Pathways, but each individual Begotten only presides over a single chunk of territory in that resonates with their Legend and the kind of world-spanning leaps enabled by random jumps are explicitly one of the things that's listed as a <i>story hook for what the Incarnate might bring to a game</i>.<br /> <br /> They're key to the ability to access and invoke the Lair, but there is a world of difference between &quot;You are mechanically encouraged to repeat the activities that spawned one of your Chambers in similar locations to expand the range of areas in which you can easily invoke Lair Traits and merge with your Horror&quot; and &quot;Despite being the first new supernatural splat since Changeling to have no innate or trivially inexpensive linguistic workaround and despite having an entire suite of powers that work based on the reinforcement of your established legend, you can hypothetically jump to a completely foreign country and nearly strand yourself because for some reason having no idea what you're doing is more likely to get you somewhere than attempting to use the fact that you are innately connected to a basement to jump to the basement in a house you know of but have never visited.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is disingenuous, given that the section you're talking about applies as much to highly faithful replicas as to the original location, immediately goes on to specify that some Beasts outright move manmade structures that they've used as Chambers elsewhere to make use of the ease of passage they present, and is the first and only item on the list to describe the penalty in more detail than &quot;a penalty.&quot;<br /> <br /> Elfive's bowed out, so now the same question apparently falls to you: What is the thematic purpose of allowing any given Beast to hop halfway across the world to a place they've almost certainly never been by sheer probability, given that Beasts are territorial legendary monsters and not Saboteur Unchained casting the widest possible net for Behind the Curtain?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Disingenuous? I say I'm not persuaded and your response is to be hostile to me, insult me by accusing me of being insincere with my argument and then try to foist off a blatantly dismissive loaded question you wanted someone else to answer who didn't want to put up with your responses anymore?<br /> <br /> Holy shit, you're just the cherry on top of this gorgeous day. Fine.<br /> <br /> In response to your first paragraph, I actually addressed this. You're making the mistake of mixing up the two sections and treating them as if they're addressing the same thing. They are not. One section is addressing the rules for opening a Primordial Pathway and the other section is addressing imposing Lair Traits and how similarity to your Chambers matters to that. The section that explicitly addresses opening Primordial Pathways says that you can only open Pathways between your Lair and somewhere else if the resonance permits. Your Lair Traits are descriptive of the resonance of your Lair. Your Chambers are referenced only as a benefit that you get, in that opening a Primordial Pathway at the exact location represented by one of your Chambers means you do not need to spend 1 Willpower and get +1 die to the roll (and +1 die for each Lair Trait applicable in the area). Otherwise, you can use similar locations (similar locations as in, anywhere that is resonant with your Lair, not similar locations to your Chambers) by spending 1 Willpower and accepting the -3 dice penalty of &quot;The external end of the Pathway is in the material world (other than the area corresponding to the Chamber)&quot;, along with any +1 die for each Lair Trait in the area. Please note that the Situation Modifier for this penalty only concerns itself where &quot;the external end of the Pathway is in the material world&quot; and it's NOT a Chamber. Either you're opening a Primordial Pathway in a location of a Chamber, or you're not. Regardless, how resonant the area is to your Lair is what really gives you bonus dice, which means Lair Traits. This section is self contained. It does not reference other sections (besides p. 99 for merging with your Horror).<br /> <br /> (Side Note: The Gorged Condition does not do what you seem to think it does. Gorged provides a +2 die bonus for opening Primordial Pathways, but only to and from the particular Chamber that your Horror is lounging in. This bonus is only for opening Primordial Pathways and therefore does not provide this bonus for the Impose Trait roll.)<br /> <br /> In response to your second paragraph, please take note that there is no penalty for distance. A Beast can go anywhere in the world that they like, so long they can find a location that is resonant with their Lair. A Beast can have Chambers throughout the material world, if they like. Nothing stops this. Beasts are worldwalkers and planeswalkers. They are explorers and seekers. They are tied to a territory, but that territory is always with them and is always within reach, no matter where they go. Because of this, Beasts can never be stranded. They can always find their way to their Lair. Having Chambers in locations you prefer really does help in making travel easier, though.<br /> <br /> In response to your third paragraph... I see that you completely stripped out all context to respond to just that one line and use it to insult me. Further, you don't actually say anything that can be responded to. Yes, the section of Chambers and Lair Traits does say in the &quot;Exact&quot; subsection that some Beasts are willing to move entire buildings that represent their Chamber to another location. I don't see an argument here. Well, no argument other than belittling me.<br /> <br /> In response to your fourth paragraph, I have a better understanding of why Elfive bowed out and I'm questioning my life choices right now. But sure, why the hell not.<br /> <br /> The question you want answered (I've taken the liberty of paraphrasing to actually keep the topic to Beast): &quot;What is the thematic purpose of allowing any given Beast to hop halfway across the world to a place they've almost certainly never been by sheer probability, given that Beasts are territorial legendary monsters?&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 65 of the book, &quot;Delving In Darkness&quot; is the section you should read. Relevant lines are &quot;The world is riddled with veins of occult lore, and Beasts believe their Mother had a hand filling them all. Unearthing those secrets grants her Children the guidance they so sorely need in her absence.&quot; and &quot;Beasts explore the world to expand their domains.&quot; The thematic purpose is written in the book itself, to promote exploration, study and understanding. Beasts are territorial legendary monsters, but their Lair is always with them.<br /> <br /> I wasn't being facetious when I said that Primordial Pathways are probably the most powerful ability Beasts have.<br /> <br /> This is a fully responsive answer. Between the previous post and this post, I don't want to get more into this with you. If you do not find this persuasive, then I'm sorry I was not able to convince you. Good day.<br /> <br /> Fuck me and fuck today. I'm having a drink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":".  Edited to add Satchel's quote. 11-19-2016, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T01:32:46-08:00","id":1005278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005243#post1005243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The max is -6 from two -3, and it seems avoidable by just keeping your story on point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not a smart man, so I will ask for clarification on this point - this seems to imply that your interpretation includes the assertion that the penalties on page 97 and those on page 101-102 do not stack.<br /> <br /> I understand you were addressing the argument of the merits of a 'random' jump and a targeted one, and the use of the Lair as a fast-travel system versus an actual narrative 'Lair', but I'm having trouble unpacking your post further (that may be because I just woke up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:53:18-08:00","id":1005371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005278#post1005278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not a smart man, so I will ask for clarification on this point - this seems to imply that your interpretation includes the assertion that the penalties on page 97 and those on page 101-102 do not stack.<br /> <br /> I understand you were addressing the argument of the merits of a 'random' jump and a targeted one, and the use of the Lair as a fast-travel system versus an actual narrative 'Lair', but I'm having trouble unpacking your post further (that may be because I just woke up).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might be a little erroneous to think of the use of the Lair as a &quot;fast-travel system&quot;. From what I'm understanding of what ArcaneArts' point, is that the Lair exists as a narrative that fits your Horror. The Lair Traits are expressions of &quot;These are the dangers that are where these monsters lurk&quot;. Yetis in blizzards, krakens during turbulent seas, dragons during thunderstorms. As darkness falls in the forest to a pitch black, monstrous wolves roam and hunt, so close your doors and huddle up to your fires.<br /> <br /> Your Lair doesn't actually exist as a real location. There is no actual correspondence between a Lair and a geographical point on Earth. The Primordial Dream just exists and is everywhere and nowhere at the same time. Due to this, it's the resonance of your Lair, the evocative expression of the dangers your Horror represents and has as it's calling cards (rumbling cracks of thunder, the fall of blinding darkness, the silence that falls and all you hear is your own heartbeat getting faster) that let you touch your Lair to real world geography, because those evocative elements are the herald to your Horror's arrival that people dread.<br /> <br /> Functionally, to your Beast... It can be a fast-travel system. But to the Beast's Horror, it's not really, because to the Yeti Horror, any place that's being covered with a howling blizzard is the outskirts of it's Lair, whether thats in the Himalaya's or in North Dakota.<br /> <br /> Did I make sense there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:53:44-08:00","id":1005372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005278#post1005278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not a smart man, so I will ask for clarification on this point - this seems to imply that your interpretation includes the assertion that the penalties on page 97 and those on page 101-102 do not stack.<br /> <br /> I understand you were addressing the argument of the merits of a 'random' jump and a targeted one, and the use of the Lair as a fast-travel system versus an actual narrative 'Lair', but I'm having trouble unpacking your post further (that may be because I just woke up).</div> </div> </div> </div><s>That would be because I am saying that-they are two separate rolls that happen to use the same stats. One is for opening the Primordial Pathways, one is for introducing Lair Traits where absolute none exist.</s>EDIT: Nope, nevermind, I was wrong.<br /> <br /> THese two things are inter-related on a metaphysical scale, in much the same way that adding Chambers is-different manifestations of the broad concept at work to provide variety of challenge and dimension and a whole lot of things-but when you get to playing, no, you're not supposed to use one for the other.<br /> <br /> A random to jump to a place you've never been is silly-<i>archmages</i> don't get that much leeway- and given the nature of doing as Beasts, places you can jump to are probably places you've been feeding in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-19-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:09:27-08:00","id":1005379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005371#post1005371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it might be a little erroneous to think of the use of the Lair as a &quot;fast-travel system&quot;. From what I'm understanding of what ArcaneArts' point, is that the Lair exists as a narrative that fits your Horror. The Lair Traits are expressions of &quot;These are the dangers that are where these monsters lurk&quot;. Yetis in blizzards, krakens during turbulent seas, dragons during thunderstorms. As darkness falls in the forest to a pitch black, monstrous wolves roam and hunt, so close your doors and huddle up to your fires.<br /> <br /> Your Lair doesn't actually exist as a real location. There is no actual correspondence between a Lair and a geographical point on Earth. The Primordial Dream just exists and is everywhere and nowhere at the same time. Due to this, it's the resonance of your Lair, the evocative expression of the dangers your Horror represents and has as it's calling cards (rumbling cracks of thunder, the fall of blinding darkness, the silence that falls and all you hear is your own heartbeat getting faster) that let you touch your Lair to real world geography, because those evocative elements are the herald to your Horror's arrival that people dread.<br /> <br /> Functionally, to your Beast... It can be a fast-travel system. But to the Beast's Horror, it's not really, because to the Yeti Horror, any place that's being covered with a howling blizzard is the outskirts of it's Lair, whether thats in the Himalaya's or in North Dakota.<br /> <br /> Did I make sense there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elegant and eloquent explanation. Alliteration intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:11:18-08:00","id":1005381,"title":"","content":"Notice: I was wrong, formatting was weird, those penalties are in reference to one another. Stupid Layout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:43:29-08:00","id":1005387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005372#post1005372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A random to jump to a place you've never been is silly-<i>archmages</i> don't get that much leeway- and given the nature of doing as Beasts, places you can jump to are probably places you've been feeding in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing how it's silly. The section for Primordial Pathways provides no consideration for distance. Considerations given are &quot;somewhere random&quot;, &quot;within a specified world&quot; and &quot;but still resonant&quot;. That can be a location practically anywhere on Earth.<br /> <br /> Archmages don't function like Beasts. They have different scopes to their power and different considerations for when their power is applicable (such as having sympathy or resonance). Beasts are a lot more restricted than Archmages in what they can do, but in their area of capability, Beasts are quite powerful. An Archmage that doesn't know the Death Arcanum isn't going to have any luck using magic to open an Avernian Gate to the Underworld, but ANY Beast can try if they know it's there.<br /> <br /> Now, for practical purposes of running a game, the ST can just have a random location be near the usual stomping grounds for the campaign if there's no interest in doing world exploring but that's a matter about what helps the campaign and story move forward. But this very much fits the theme of exploration that Beast has. Being able to go to a random location that fits the resonance of your Lair is an opportunity to explore and discover new things, whether that random location is a section of the city you call home that you haven't visited much or whether that random location is somewhere more exotic and unknown. The Beast doesn't get to decide, that doesn't mean the ST and the Beast's Player can't share ideas and decide what sounds more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:44:56-08:00","id":1005388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005381#post1005381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stupid Layout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you believe those penalties were intended to stack the way they do, and editing/layout butchered that presentation? Or do you think they were meant to not having anything to do with each other, and the remaining references are an editing artifact?<br /> <br /> (or something else entirely?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:50:56-08:00","id":1005391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1005388#post1005388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe those penalties were intended to stack the way they do, and editing/layout butchered that presentation? Or do you think they were meant to not having anything to do with each other, and the remaining references are an editing artifact?<br /> <br /> (or something else entirely?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not able to determine what ArcaneArts means, either. Citing that the penalty only goes up to -6 suggests that the charts from both pages don't interact with each other. But then ArcaneArts states that they're in reference to each other which is... contradictory, I think.<br /> <br /> If they were in reference to each other, wouldn't they have a page citation of where to go? That's usually how the book treats references to other sections and pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:44:21-08:00","id":1006007,"title":"","content":"Taking cues from Arc's playbook here and just straight-up writing a pseudo-essay.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Why It Is Important That Chamber Resonance Applies To Primordial Pathway Rolls: A Micro-Dissertation</b></u><br /> <br /> Going through the key issues in no particular order\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>1. If It Doesn't Apply, Other Beast Template Features Are Made Inferior and/or Redundant</b>.<br /> If you can open a Pathway to or from anywhere (or even &quot;just&quot; anywhere with a Lair Trait belonging to you or your broodmates), Skeleton Key and Under the Bed are absurdly involved, restrictive, and/or expensive to use \u2014 why bother seeking out supernatural gateways when jumping to your Lair or the Shadow of your current location is as simple as opening a Pathway and maybe switching Chambers?<br /> If you can open a Pathway anywhere, you can overlap your Lair with anyplace \u2014 and your Lair offers all the benefits that imposing Lair Traits does and more without having to spend Satiety. (Imposing Lair Traits from scratch is already slightly lessened in utility by the ability to cause some of them [and thus become able to invoke the rest without a roll] with Atavisms or basic preparation like setting off the sprinklers or turning out the lights.)<br /> <br /> <b>2. If It Doesn't Apply, Half the Benefits of Incarnation Are A Booby Prize.</b><br /> If you can open a Primordial Pathway from anywhere, that means you can enter your Lair and assume a monstrous form from anywhere \u2014 and that's a description of two of the more interpersonally relevant traits the Beast Incarnate universally possesses (shaving off half the downsides of Satiety is desirable, yes, but it doesn't do anybody else any good unless they're also seeking Incarnation) without the drawback of Destabilization and the potential geographic constraint of staying the Apex of a given hive to worry about.<br /> <br /> <b>3. If It Doesn't Apply, Multiple Example Characters Have To Be Supremely Unimaginative and/or Idiots.</b><br /> The Eastside Pyro is starving and in prison. Boleslav is an Incarnate who rules over a small village. The vast majority of Beast's inspirational critters and example characters are quite regionally particular (the hodag is largely unheard of outside of Wisconsin, for example), and yet somehow the vast majority of Beasts do not simply pull up stakes and vanish to another district/city/state/country through the Lair when their activities come back to them. Speaking of which\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>4. If It Doesn't Apply, There's No Reason to Eat at Home.</b><br /> It's not hard for Beasts to figure out how to scare people \u2014 they tend to embody and/or dwell in the kinds of things that terrify regardless of regional specifics, so foreign cultures and the language barrier don't usually stop them from feeding.<br /> So if you can just open a Pathway to anywhere on Earth and it's not significantly harder to reach a place that you haven't personally sowed nightmares in, what actually stops you as a young Beast from disappearing to a faraway land and eating random strangers without any repercussions for your personal life?<br /> <br /> <b>5. If It Doesn't Apply, Slumbering is Narratively Toothless and Your Lair is the Most Insecure Secure Location Around.</b><br /> If your Heart's lack of correspondence to a material location has no interaction with the rules for Chamber resonance, you should by definition be able to open a Pathway straight to your Horror at Satiety 10 and inflict the requisite scratch damage without having to collapse a Chamber, put yourself near death, or brave the hazards of your Lair first.<br /> &quot;Another Beast's Lair&quot; is part of the subset of the cosmology that it is unambiguously the easiest to open a Primordial Pathway to \u2014 there is no &quot;except for the Heart&quot; clause there, so any Beast who knows you're a Beast can harry you at the core of your stronghold without any extra difficulty whatsoever under this interpretation.<br /> <br /> <b>6. You're Playing a Sympathetic Monster Even if the Word &quot;Sympathy&quot; Isn't Directly Used, and That Matters.</b><br /> The random-location option works on the basis that the Primordial Dream touches every place in the perceivable cosmos through resonance. Resonance <i>is sympathy</i> \u2014 the mystical/emotional/physical principle of like-attracts-like is one of the most basic organizing principles of supernatural ecology, echoed everywhere from the Shadow to the convergent evolution of the Kindred, and Astral domains like the Primordial Dream embody it most strongly thanks to not being constrained by material geography \u2014 and sympathy is variable in ways that have to do with more than just what world you're in \u2014 whether you agree about their applicability to Pathways or not, that's why the penalties from Chamber resonance apply to attempts to invoke Lair Traits from nothing.<br /> The Primordial Dream does not have a substantially stronger connection to &quot;everywhere&quot; than &quot;the immanent magical center of all things&quot; and its denizens claim relation to a number of monsters that <i>do</i> engage with sympathy, so the idea that they arbitrarily don't make use of sympathetic connections in more than the absolute broadest sense of shared-phenomenon doesn't have a lot of heft to it.<br /> The random-location option's social analogue is Thicker Than Water \u2014 in the absence of repulsive circumstances, every Beast can <i>potentially</i> get along with any monster they encounter and eventually develop Family Ties with them, but mere universal Kinship (and Kinship is <i>also</i> a form of sympathy) doesn't give a Beast Family Ties with every monster in existence, much less draw them all to you from across the pond. You have to build up the connection to be able to reach the point where that monster is better at helping you and vice versa than other monsters, and if Chamber resonance doesn't apply to travel then it becomes substantially less likely that the sort of circumstances that lend support to &quot;You don't choose your family&quot; as a theme come up.<br /> <br /> <b>7. Exploration Does Not Exist in a Vacuum.</b><br /> Most explorers in common thought do not blink from island to island and jigsaw their maps together as they stumble across common elements. Most explorers travel some unknown direction in relation to defined routes and mark the terrain they pass through to assemble a more cohesive view of the world. (Sometimes they also plant flags, which are usually more helpful if you can reasonably expect your enemies and countrymen to reach the same place as you without your guidance.)<br /> I find it really hard to play a convincing explorer when I have Farthest Shores Landing Prana.<br /> <br /> <b>8. Other Games Equip Their Characters For Dives Into Foreign Parts When It's Appropriate.</b><br /> <i>a. Born With It</i><br /> Werewolves and Sin-Eaters both have inherent workarounds for potential language barriers in their respective chunks of the cosmos (speaking the native tongue and having a universal translator for the dead, respectively) and possess innate means of keyless entry through those domains' entrances. Any werewolf can talk with any spirit in any part of the world, regardless of whether the spirit has learned any of the Uratha's human languages or indeed has ever been outside of the peak of an ancient mountain on the outskirts of rural India, and the Bound don't need to worry about the fact that a ghost from the age of the Crusades only speaks the great-grandparent of a living tongue and dwells behind a secret gate in the basement of an office building in Istanbul. Neither of these character types would be capable of handling the other's situation with the same ease, because their gamelines do not assume that werewolves will routinely need to deal with ghosts in the Deep Dominions or that Sin-Eaters will have much of any truck with the Shadow of a secluded mountain wilderness.<br /> Demons and Mummies both have reason to find themselves far away from their last known location and needing to integrate with mortal society on short notice, and they have linguistic shortcuts to facilitate this capacity to be in four wildly different countries in the course of a decade. Demons have perfect memories and total control of normally unconscious tics and processes, the ability to steal or fabricate mortal identities and shed them in an evidence-shredding flash of brilliance, and native fluency in pretty much every language you'd encounter on the street in any part of the world; seeing as they're fugitives hiding from God under Its own nose, they need to be able to bug out fast and deflect suspicion in short order. Mummies are served by cults whose existences essentially parallel the development of civilization, they wake up with only a small amount of self-knowledge at the beginning of a given descent, and they could well have been inactive for over a century depending on the circumstances; fortunately, even though their most common task requires very little in the way of communications, they can pick up new languages over the course of a lunch break and most of their cults have at least one member who speaks their ancient language.<br /> <br /> <i>b. Work For It</i><br /> Mages and Prometheans both kind of have to build for dives into faraway countries or other dimensions, but they have some shortcuts where it's relevant. Prometheans switch Refinements with some regularity, and the one that deals with human interaction as a focus needs no special consideration to start following and includes a universal translator effect in one of its signature Alembics, which can be retained after leaving the Refinement with a small investment of resources only a bit more involved than learning new languages the long way (and there's an Alembic that can theoretically shortcut that in two other Refinements' sets, including the one focused on interaction with other supernatural beings) \u2014 the Created are encouraged to wander from place to place, and if one of those places happens to pose a language barrier, they can adapt themselves to surmount it. Meanwhile, mages have &quot;speak with [native ephemeral being]&quot; spells become available before &quot;open gateway to [supernatural dimension]&quot; spells in the Arcana relating to those worlds by virtue of the basic progression of spell knowledge (the same level of expertise in another Subtle Arcanum allows you to be understood by anybody as long as you're telling the truth), any one of them can convey meaning to anyone who isn't a vanilla mortal even without formal training, and the Path with the most talent for regular worldly teleportation also has a natural affinity for telepathy and universal linguistic translation \u2014 the Awakened are consummate investigators whose reach sometimes exceeds their grasp, and the structure of their powers is such that dealing with the expected outcome of a given journey is usually within their ability by the simple virtue of their being powerful enough to make that journey.<br /> Changelings and Vampires are mentally and metaphysically incentivized by their lost humanity to either keep to their established haunts in and around the section of the mortal world they live in or specialize their (un)lifestyles toward being nomadic, largely on the basis of known threats being more manageable than unknown threats and sudden surprises being detrimental to their grasp of humanity and current events. Nothing stops them from learning new languages or acquire mortal or mystical interpreters, and they have a great deal of extra time to do so, but the niche their default society operates under is typically very local on account of it offering better security and not needing to lean too much on supernatural powers to stop people from asking about the new stranger in their midst and/or where all the thumbtacks went.<br /> <br /> <i>c. The Takeaway</i><br /> Beasts fall conceptually closest to changelings and vampires in terms of innate cultural integration skills and their extradimensional nexus-point corresponds to their location and experience most strongly; the vast majority of them aren't on the run from angels or Huntsmen or Disquiet, without outside interference they're living beings who experience time as a daily procession of occurrences between periods of sleep, and generally speaking the Devouring doesn't grant them any heightened ability to understand what people from different worlds and eras are saying, so either Beasts are supposed to be able to make contact with complete strangers without preamble and vanish just as quickly with no meaningful entanglement resulting or the game is set up in such a manner that the expected playstyle uses good old-fashioned legwork and local guides as the principle means of exploration from the known into the unknown.<br /> <br /> That's about two and a half hours of rambling type in points of of wildly varying length that still doesn't go into a whole lot of detail, but there it is. I'll clarify particulars if asked, but as it stands I have a substantial backlog of media I just spent two hours not catching up on, so up the listicle goes with special emphasis given to Points 1-4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T00:45:21-08:00","id":1006043,"title":"","content":"Beasts Adam and Betty share a Brood Lair.<br /> <br /> Adam finds a location that has descriptive similarity to one of the chambers in their Lair - this particular chamber is in his 'side' of the Lair. He imposes three of his other Lair Traits in the area, for a total of 4 active Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> Betty does the same, attempting to help him open a Pathway so they can both retreat to their Lair. Multi-part question:<br /> <br /> 1) Does Adam have +4 from Lair Traits, or +7 (with +3 coming from Betty's imposed traits)? The game seems to treat Brood Lairs as a singular Lair in some respects, and as loose connection of Lairs in others.<br /> <br /> 2) If Adam only has +4, does the answer to #1 change if it's a chamber shared between both of them?<br /> <br /> 3) If Adam is in the Brood Lair, and moves to one of Betty's Chambers, can he open a Pathway from that Chamber to its physical reflection? If so, does he get the usual +1 Bonus for using the corresponding physical location?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:17:17-08:00","id":1006052,"title":"","content":"If the book instructs you to use the penalties from differing similarity found on Page 101 of the book under the section titled &quot;Chambers and Lair Traits&quot; when making the roll for opening a Pathway as described under &quot;Primordial Pathways&quot; on Pages 97-98, then it would make a lot of sense for the book to say so by citing the title of the relevant section and what page it is on. Like on Page 88 under Family Resemblance it says &quot;(expressed by their Supernatural Tolerance rating; see pg. 222)&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only page number I see referenced under &quot;Primordial Pathways&quot; is to pg. 99, for merging with your Horror. Is there an updated version of the book that points to page 101 under the section &quot;Primordial Pathways&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:33:43-08:00","id":1006061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006043#post1006043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts Adam and Betty share a Brood Lair.<br /> <br /> Adam finds a location that has descriptive similarity to one of the chambers in their Lair - this particular chamber is in his 'side' of the Lair. He imposes three of his other Lair Traits in the area, for a total of 4 active Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> Betty does the same, attempting to help him open a Pathway so they can both retreat to their Lair. Multi-part question:<br /> <br /> 1) Does Adam have +4 from Lair Traits, or +7 (with +3 coming from Betty's imposed traits)? The game seems to treat Brood Lairs as a singular Lair in some respects, and as loose connection of Lairs in others.<br /> <br /> 2) If Adam only has +4, does the answer to #1 change if it's a chamber shared between both of them?<br /> <br /> 3) If Adam is in the Brood Lair, and moves to one of Betty's Chambers, can he open a Pathway from that Chamber to its physical reflection? If so, does he get the usual +1 Bonus for using the corresponding physical location?</div> </div> </div> </div>From reading Brood Lairs on page 96.... This what I think the answers are likely to be.<br /> <br /> 1) Assuming the Traits that Adam uses and that Betty uses are all different Traits, Adam gets +7. Brood Lairs states that Beasts with a Brood Lair gain access to all of the Traits the combined Lairs have.<br /> <br /> 2) Don't think sharing a Chamber affects that.<br /> <br /> 3) I don't think Adam can open a Pathway from one of Betty's Chambers to it's physical reflection, because that Chamber isn't technically part of his Lair.<br /> <br /> Having access to more Trait options and being able to help each other defend the Brood Lair seems like the two big benefits of having one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:28:10-08:00","id":1006075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https: