tiety is desirable, yes, but it doesn't do anybody else any good unless they're also seeking Incarnation) without the drawback of Destabilization and the potential geographic constraint of staying the Apex of a given hive to worry about.<br /> <br /> <b>3. If It Doesn't Apply, Multiple Example Characters Have To Be Supremely Unimaginative and/or Idiots.</b><br /> The Eastside Pyro is starving and in prison. Boleslav is an Incarnate who rules over a small village. The vast majority of Beast's inspirational critters and example characters are quite regionally particular (the hodag is largely unheard of outside of Wisconsin, for example), and yet somehow the vast majority of Beasts do not simply pull up stakes and vanish to another district/city/state/country through the Lair when their activities come back to them. Speaking of which\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>4. If It Doesn't Apply, There's No Reason to Eat at Home.</b><br /> It's not hard for Beasts to figure out how to scare people \u2014 they tend to embody and/or dwell in the kinds of things that terrify regardless of regional specifics, so foreign cultures and the language barrier don't usually stop them from feeding.<br /> So if you can just open a Pathway to anywhere on Earth and it's not significantly harder to reach a place that you haven't personally sowed nightmares in, what actually stops you as a young Beast from disappearing to a faraway land and eating random strangers without any repercussions for your personal life?<br /> <br /> <b>5. If It Doesn't Apply, Slumbering is Narratively Toothless and Your Lair is the Most Insecure Secure Location Around.</b><br /> If your Heart's lack of correspondence to a material location has no interaction with the rules for Chamber resonance, you should by definition be able to open a Pathway straight to your Horror at Satiety 10 and inflict the requisite scratch damage without having to collapse a Chamber, put yourself near death, or brave the hazards of your Lair first.<br /> &quot;Another Beast's Lair&quot; is part of the subset of the cosmology that it is unambiguously the easiest to open a Primordial Pathway to \u2014 there is no &quot;except for the Heart&quot; clause there, so any Beast who knows you're a Beast can harry you at the core of your stronghold without any extra difficulty whatsoever under this interpretation.<br /> <br /> <b>6. You're Playing a Sympathetic Monster Even if the Word &quot;Sympathy&quot; Isn't Directly Used, and That Matters.</b><br /> The random-location option works on the basis that the Primordial Dream touches every place in the perceivable cosmos through resonance. Resonance <i>is sympathy</i> \u2014 the mystical/emotional/physical principle of like-attracts-like is one of the most basic organizing principles of supernatural ecology, echoed everywhere from the Shadow to the convergent evolution of the Kindred, and Astral domains like the Primordial Dream embody it most strongly thanks to not being constrained by material geography \u2014 and sympathy is variable in ways that have to do with more than just what world you're in \u2014 whether you agree about their applicability to Pathways or not, that's why the penalties from Chamber resonance apply to attempts to invoke Lair Traits from nothing.<br /> The Primordial Dream does not have a substantially stronger connection to &quot;everywhere&quot; than &quot;the immanent magical center of all things&quot; and its denizens claim relation to a number of monsters that <i>do</i> engage with sympathy, so the idea that they arbitrarily don't make use of sympathetic connections in more than the absolute broadest sense of shared-phenomenon doesn't have a lot of heft to it.<br /> The random-location option's social analogue is Thicker Than Water \u2014 in the absence of repulsive circumstances, every Beast can <i>potentially</i> get along with any monster they encounter and eventually develop Family Ties with them, but mere universal Kinship (and Kinship is <i>also</i> a form of sympathy) doesn't give a Beast Family Ties with every monster in existence, much less draw them all to you from across the pond. You have to build up the connection to be able to reach the point where that monster is better at helping you and vice versa than other monsters, and if Chamber resonance doesn't apply to travel then it becomes substantially less likely that the sort of circumstances that lend support to &quot;You don't choose your family&quot; as a theme come up.<br /> <br /> <b>7. Exploration Does Not Exist in a Vacuum.</b><br /> Most explorers in common thought do not blink from island to island and jigsaw their maps together as they stumble across common elements. Most explorers travel some unknown direction in relation to defined routes and mark the terrain they pass through to assemble a more cohesive view of the world. (Sometimes they also plant flags, which are usually more helpful if you can reasonably expect your enemies and countrymen to reach the same place as you without your guidance.)<br /> I find it really hard to play a convincing explorer when I have Farthest Shores Landing Prana.<br /> <br /> <b>8. Other Games Equip Their Characters For Dives Into Foreign Parts When It's Appropriate.</b><br /> <i>a. Born With It</i><br /> Werewolves and Sin-Eaters both have inherent workarounds for potential language barriers in their respective chunks of the cosmos (speaking the native tongue and having a universal translator for the dead, respectively) and possess innate means of keyless entry through those domains' entrances. Any werewolf can talk with any spirit in any part of the world, regardless of whether the spirit has learned any of the Uratha's human languages or indeed has ever been outside of the peak of an ancient mountain on the outskirts of rural India, and the Bound don't need to worry about the fact that a ghost from the age of the Crusades only speaks the great-grandparent of a living tongue and dwells behind a secret gate in the basement of an office building in Istanbul. Neither of these character types would be capable of handling the other's situation with the same ease, because their gamelines do not assume that werewolves will routinely need to deal with ghosts in the Deep Dominions or that Sin-Eaters will have much of any truck with the Shadow of a secluded mountain wilderness.<br /> Demons and Mummies both have reason to find themselves far away from their last known location and needing to integrate with mortal society on short notice, and they have linguistic shortcuts to facilitate this capacity to be in four wildly different countries in the course of a decade. Demons have perfect memories and total control of normally unconscious tics and processes, the ability to steal or fabricate mortal identities and shed them in an evidence-shredding flash of brilliance, and native fluency in pretty much every language you'd encounter on the street in any part of the world; seeing as they're fugitives hiding from God under Its own nose, they need to be able to bug out fast and deflect suspicion in short order. Mummies are served by cults whose existences essentially parallel the development of civilization, they wake up with only a small amount of self-knowledge at the beginning of a given descent, and they could well have been inactive for over a century depending on the circumstances; fortunately, even though their most common task requires very little in the way of communications, they can pick up new languages over the course of a lunch break and most of their cults have at least one member who speaks their ancient language.<br /> <br /> <i>b. Work For It</i><br /> Mages and Prometheans both kind of have to build for dives into faraway countries or other dimensions, but they have some shortcuts where it's relevant. Prometheans switch Refinements with some regularity, and the one that deals with human interaction as a focus needs no special consideration to start following and includes a universal translator effect in one of its signature Alembics, which can be retained after leaving the Refinement with a small investment of resources only a bit more involved than learning new languages the long way (and there's an Alembic that can theoretically shortcut that in two other Refinements' sets, including the one focused on interaction with other supernatural beings) \u2014 the Created are encouraged to wander from place to place, and if one of those places happens to pose a language barrier, they can adapt themselves to surmount it. Meanwhile, mages have &quot;speak with [native ephemeral being]&quot; spells become available before &quot;open gateway to [supernatural dimension]&quot; spells in the Arcana relating to those worlds by virtue of the basic progression of spell knowledge (the same level of expertise in another Subtle Arcanum allows you to be understood by anybody as long as you're telling the truth), any one of them can convey meaning to anyone who isn't a vanilla mortal even without formal training, and the Path with the most talent for regular worldly teleportation also has a natural affinity for telepathy and universal linguistic translation \u2014 the Awakened are consummate investigators whose reach sometimes exceeds their grasp, and the structure of their powers is such that dealing with the expected outcome of a given journey is usually within their ability by the simple virtue of their being powerful enough to make that journey.<br /> Changelings and Vampires are mentally and metaphysically incentivized by their lost humanity to either keep to their established haunts in and around the section of the mortal world they live in or specialize their (un)lifestyles toward being nomadic, largely on the basis of known threats being more manageable than unknown threats and sudden surprises being detrimental to their grasp of humanity and current events. Nothing stops them from learning new languages or acquire mortal or mystical interpreters, and they have a great deal of extra time to do so, but the niche their default society operates under is typically very local on account of it offering better security and not needing to lean too much on supernatural powers to stop people from asking about the new stranger in their midst and/or where all the thumbtacks went.<br /> <br /> <i>c. The Takeaway</i><br /> Beasts fall conceptually closest to changelings and vampires in terms of innate cultural integration skills and their extradimensional nexus-point corresponds to their location and experience most strongly; the vast majority of them aren't on the run from angels or Huntsmen or Disquiet, without outside interference they're living beings who experience time as a daily procession of occurrences between periods of sleep, and generally speaking the Devouring doesn't grant them any heightened ability to understand what people from different worlds and eras are saying, so either Beasts are supposed to be able to make contact with complete strangers without preamble and vanish just as quickly with no meaningful entanglement resulting or the game is set up in such a manner that the expected playstyle uses good old-fashioned legwork and local guides as the principle means of exploration from the known into the unknown.<br /> <br /> That's about two and a half hours of rambling type in points of of wildly varying length that still doesn't go into a whole lot of detail, but there it is. I'll clarify particulars if asked, but as it stands I have a substantial backlog of media I just spent two hours not catching up on, so up the listicle goes with special emphasis given to Points 1-4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaand I'm sold. I ended up glossing and skimming over the past few pages because for some reason people were using page references of a book already known to have not-so-perfect formatting, and taking offenses personally to the point a normally sound discussion was turning into a hellhole, but this trumps everything in my eyes.<br /> <br /> Sympathy is the most consistent and powerful aspect of magic, both in the CofD games and in real life traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T03:19:02-08:00","id":1006092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006075#post1006075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aaaand I'm sold. I ended up glossing and skimming over the past few pages because for some reason people were using page references of a book already known to have not-so-perfect formatting, and taking offenses personally to the point a normally sound discussion was turning into a hellhole, but this trumps everything in my eyes.<br /> <br /> Sympathy is the most consistent and powerful aspect of magic, both in the CofD games and in real life traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathy does matter, though. The book says that it's the Traits of a Lair that define what resonates to your Lair. That's why it's easier to open a Pathway in a location that has one or more Traits. It resonates, and has sympathy, with your Lair.<br /> <br /> What allows you to add a location as a Chamber to your Lair? Well, either you need to have rolled an exceptional success on a Nightmare in the area, or someone lost Integrity in the area under specific circumstances... and &quot;The environment must contain at least one element matching a Lair Trait in the Beast's Lair.&quot; With these two qualifications, the location resonates with both your Legend and the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> The book keeps coming back to Lair Traits for a reason.<br /> <br /> Also, I use page references to direct people to specific places of the book so they can see where I'm drawing the basis of my arguments from. Not-so-perfect formatting doesn't have anything to do with the actual content of the book itself, such as mechanics. The book just doesn't tell you to use those penalties for opening Pathways. If you want to add those penalties anyways, knock yourself out. I think that's more restricting on the power of Beasts than the book expects, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-21-2016, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T03:37:23-08:00","id":1006097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006092#post1006092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sympathy does matter, though. The book says that it's the Traits of a Lair that define what resonates to your Lair. That's why it's easier to open a Pathway in a location that has one or more Traits. It resonates, and has sympathy, with your Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no point to argue with that one. But still, to me using 'universal' sympathies like that (as in, something that is relatively common - a Blizzard is a Blizzard, whether it's from the snowy mountains of a yeti's dwelling or the ice-laden windy shipwreck a kraken rests in) look like something only a very powerful being should be able to, and 'lesser' beings should use more 'personal' sympathies, not because they're the only option, but because they're the easier option until they've sufficiently toughened up to the point where they can say &quot;Screw it, I'm the boss and I call the shots&quot; any time and anywhere they want. Which is why I support &quot;normal Beasts can use Lair Traits to essentially teleport, but doing so should be damn hard&quot; part of the argument<br /> <br /> Dunno if I'm making sense here, since I'm mentally tired and it's probabl that I misunderstood your arguments, or the arguments of one of you (or even <i>all </i>of you) at one point or the other. Correct me ruthlessly if I got something wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T03:58:27-08:00","id":1006104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006092#post1006092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book just doesn't tell you to use those penalties for opening Pathways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Penalties to opening Primordial Pathways are explicitly mentioned in all four sections describing the levels of similarity on p101 to p102. Is your argument that the penalties are only relevant for opening Pathways because they determine how easy it is to impose Lair Traits ex nihilo, which builds resonance for the actual opening of the Pathway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T04:18:38-08:00","id":1006112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006097#post1006097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, no point to argue with that one. But still, to me using 'universal' sympathies like that (as in, something that is relatively common - a Blizzard is a Blizzard, whether it's from the snowy mountains of a yeti's dwelling or the ice-laden windy shipwreck a kraken rests in) look like something only a very powerful being should be able to, and 'lesser' beings should use more 'personal' sympathies, not because they're the only option, but because they're the easier option until they've sufficiently toughened up to the point where they can say &amp;quot;Screw it, I'm the boss and I call the shots&amp;quot; any time and anywhere they want. Which is why I support &amp;quot;normal Beasts can use Lair Traits to essentially teleport, but doing so should be damn hard&amp;quot; part of the argument<br /> <br /> Dunno if I'm making sense here, since I'm mentally tired and it's probabl that I misunderstood your arguments, or the arguments of one of you (or even <i>all </i>of you) at one point or the other. Correct me ruthlessly if I got something wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Think of this. Calling it &quot;teleporting&quot; is reductive and dismissive. This isn't essentially teleporting, it's taking shortcuts available to you because you are a monster of nightmares where space has no meaning. What matters to you isn't distance, but the kind of connection you have to a place. Your Lair serves as a nexus point to any of these locations. You're not teleporting, you're taking a road that others just don't have access to. If you had a big graveyard theme to your Lair, is it really out of place to think you can show up at any graveyard? Does it matter where the graveyard is? Whether it's in China or Mexico? People dread the dead regardless of where they live.<br /> <br /> I think you're overlooking how limiting random Pathways are, too. Beasts can either go to a precise location they know of or a random location. That's pretty limiting! Especially as Satchel is correct in that Beasts don't have much stuff to help them blend in with human cultures. But that's not very surprising considering they're nightmare monsters. But it's not like a Beast just can't learn a language in their travels. The thing is, they'll always want to find Chambers and those absolutely better tie them to specific locations, which they'll want to hang out around simply because it's easier. <br /> <br /> Finally, regarding power... Think of this. You're already acknowledging that a Beast can call up a blizzard when they want to. How does that fit in with other supernatural creatures? How powerful is that?<br /> <br /> Beasts have an Atavism that lets them spew out fire for no cost. Beasts are meant to be powerful in their box. But it's still a box and they don't have any of the flexibility Mages can show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T04:33:47-08:00","id":1006116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006104#post1006104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penalties to opening Primordial Pathways are explicitly mentioned in all four sections describing the levels of similarity on p101 to p102. Is your argument that the penalties are only relevant for opening Pathways because they determine how easy it is to impose Lair Traits ex nihilo, which builds resonance for the actual opening of the Pathway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. My interpretation there is that its the Beasts goal to open a Pathway in that location (I think they use this motivation because it's easier than providing an example for a combat context, the other major reason you'd want to impose Traits), and they're trying to make the location more resonant with their Lair to make opening the Pathway easier. Which is relevant to the topic of the mechanics of imposing Traits.<br /> <br /> And it makes sense to me why you'd want to. A -3 penalty on a Wits + Resolve roll for a starting character really sucks, especially when you have to burn Willpower for it. <br /> <br /> And it costs you a Willpower point to impose a Trait too!<br /> <br /> 2 Willpower to gain access to your Lair without being picky seems like a fair price, honestly. A Beast won't want to do that often. That's why Chambers are so useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T04:58:57-08:00","id":1006123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006112#post1006112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... Think of this. Calling it &quot;teleporting&quot; is reductive and dismissive. This isn't essentially teleporting, it's taking shortcuts available to you because you are a monster of nightmares where space has no meaning. What matters to you isn't distance, but the kind of connection you have to a place. Your Lair serves as a nexus point to any of these locations. You're not teleporting, you're taking a road that others just don't have access to. If you had a big graveyard theme to your Lair, is it really out of place to think you can show up at any graveyard? Does it matter where the graveyard is? Whether it's in China or Mexico? People dread the dead regardless of where they live.<br /> <br /> I think you're overlooking how limiting random Pathways are, too. Beasts can either go to a precise location they know of or a random location. That's pretty limiting! Especially as Satchel is correct in that Beasts don't have much stuff to help them blend in with human cultures. But that's not very surprising considering they're nightmare monsters. But it's not like a Beast just can't learn a language in their travels. The thing is, they'll always want to find Chambers and those absolutely better tie them to specific locations, which they'll want to hang out around simply because it's easier.<br /> <br /> Finally, regarding power... Think of this. You're already acknowledging that a Beast can call up a blizzard when they want to. How does that fit in with other supernatural creatures? How powerful is that?<br /> <br /> Beasts have an Atavism that lets them spew out fire for no cost. Beasts are meant to be powerful in their box. But it's still a box and they don't have any of the flexibility Mages can show.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a <i>very </i>convincing argument. Still, I stand by that having access to a road no one can even perceive doesn't make walking that road easier. Afterall, even if you know a way around the rifts that no landlubber would know, you still have to brave the winds to actually sail through them. But I'm all for Beasts doing whatever they can to <i>make </i>the road easier.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T05:09:40-08:00","id":1006127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006123#post1006123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a <i>very </i>convincing argument. Still, I stand by that having access to a road no one can even perceive doesn't make walking that road easier. Afterall, even if you know a way around the rifts that no landlubber would know, you still have to brave the winds to actually sail through them. But I'm all for Beasts doing whatever they can to <i>make </i>the road easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm rather curious here... What do you think is so easy about a Wits + Resolve roll that faces a -6 or possibly a -5 dice penalty for a location you have no control over? <br /> <br /> Isn't &quot;go somewhere random&quot; essentially a Storyteller tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T05:24:29-08:00","id":1006138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006127#post1006127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm rather curious here... What do you think is so easy about a Wits + Resolve roll that faces a -6 or possibly a -5 dice penalty for a location you have no control over?<br /> <br /> Isn't &quot;go somewhere random&quot; essentially a Storyteller tool?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to think about that one. I'm afraid I can't answer you without a lot of bluffing and shooting in the dark, because I'm terribly weak on crunch. And I don't want to disservice you by trying to argue on something I don't have full comprehension over, or at least as much as understanding as you do. I'll come back only after I read up a bit more on this - which might be after this thread withers away, because I have exams coming up and I badly need to study.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T05:33:46-08:00","id":1006148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006138#post1006138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll have to think about that one. I'm afraid I can't answer you without a lot of bluffing and shooting in the dark, because I'm terribly weak on crunch. And I don't want to disservice you by trying to argue on something I don't have full comprehension over, or at least as much as understanding as you do. I'll come back only after I read up a bit more on this - which might be after this thread withers away, because I have exams coming up and I badly need to study.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps... <br /> <br /> Wits and Resolve are both Attributes. A starting Beast gets one dot in all Attributes, and then you get 5/4/3 dots to assign to Mental, Social and Physical attributes. Wits and Resolve are both Mental Attributes, so if that's the primary category for someone that wants to be good at opening Primordial Pathways, you're looking at Wits 3 and Resolve 3.<br /> <br /> 6 dice to roll against a -6 or -5 dice penalty. Feel lucky? ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T06:34:53-08:00","id":1006166,"title":"","content":"While Satchel has convinced me that this is intended, I'd still like to hear from anyone that has <i>actual play</i> experience using the rules this way that still had fun using Pathways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:00:35-08:00","id":1006174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006166#post1006166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Satchel has convinced me that this is intended, I'd still like to hear from anyone that has <i>actual play</i> experience using the rules this way that still had fun using Pathways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I don't have actual play experience, and therefore can't answer that question. <br /> <br /> May I ask what in particular you found convincing from Satchel? I'm curious if there's a point I might have missed or accidentally glossed over and should reconsider to make sure I have a fair understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:52:33-08:00","id":1006190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006174#post1006174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm afraid I don't have actual play experience, and therefore can't answer that question.<br /> <br /> May I ask what in particular you found convincing from Satchel? I'm curious if there's a point I might have missed or accidentally glossed over and should reconsider to make sure I have a fair understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your posts all make good arguments for why it <i>should</i> be the other way around, but Satchel's essay, particularly points one through four, make a very convincing argument for that interpretation not meshing with the way things are presented in the books.<br /> <br /> We're probably not going to do it that way in our game, because the characters have already reached ~30XP doing the other way, and it would be inconsistent to change now - it also honestly just feels really limiting and un-fun, which is not a factor one should discard at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T09:36:36-08:00","id":1006234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006190#post1006190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your posts all make good arguments for why it <i>should</i> be the other way around, but Satchel's essay, particularly points one through four, make a very convincing argument for that interpretation not meshing with the way things are presented in the books.<br /> <br /> We're probably not going to do it that way in our game, because the characters have already reached ~30XP doing the other way, and it would be inconsistent to change now - it also honestly just feels really limiting and un-fun, which is not a factor one should discard at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I didn't answer those questions because I didn't want to have a continuous back and forth between with Satchel. I didn't think we'd convince each other. <br /> <br /> I really, strongly, suggest checking out again some of the capabilities Satchel greatly undersells. Beast Incarnate provides immense benefits, one being able to use Pathways effortlessly, at any time, anywhere, to go wherever you want, which is a huge advantage compared to needing to spend 2 willpower and likely facing a -5 dice penalty with the destination being random. And then there's being able to depower Heroes with a touch. The differences between a normal Beast and an Incarnate are vast in terms of capabilities. <br /> <br /> On never feasting where you live... I'm not sure why they think the capability to randomly wander at great cost and effort somewhere will provide a reasonable meal or why they think a Beast could do this regularly. They can't. <br /> <br /> Skeleton Key is incredibly useful because it gets you to somewhere specific. If you don't know of a precise location in the Hedge but need to get somewhere, you can of course burn twice the willpower, eat a hefty penalty and pop up somewhere random, but this is the Hedge and that's incredibly dangerous, also good luck finding where you need to go. A door to the Hedge takes you somewhere specific and that's very important. <br /> <br /> Well, I don't want to harp about it to you. Thank you for answering. ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:06:44-08:00","id":1006356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006043#post1006043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts Adam and Betty share a Brood Lair.<br /> <br /> Adam finds a location that has descriptive similarity to one of the chambers in their Lair - this particular chamber is in his 'side' of the Lair. He imposes three of his other Lair Traits in the area, for a total of 4 active Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> Betty does the same, attempting to help him open a Pathway so they can both retreat to their Lair. Multi-part question:<br /> <br /> 1) Does Adam have +4 from Lair Traits, or +7 (with +3 coming from Betty's imposed traits)? The game seems to treat Brood Lairs as a singular Lair in some respects, and as loose connection of Lairs in others.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is +4, given the specification of &quot;[\u2026]may include <b>one</b> Trait from any other Beast in the brood[\u2026]&quot; in the section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) If Adam only has +4, does the answer to #1 change if it's a chamber shared between both of them? </div> </div> </div>The bonus from Lair Traits remains consistent, though this does possibly raise the question of whether Betty would merge with her Horror while Adam's Pathway was open. (She probably would, since they share a Lair through a Chamber and are in the same physical location.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) If Adam is in the Brood Lair, and moves to one of Betty's Chambers, can he open a Pathway from that Chamber to its physical reflection? If so, does he get the usual +1 Bonus for using the corresponding physical location? </div> </div> </div>I'd say no, unless he's also got a Chamber with at least descriptive similarity to the Chamber in Betty's Lair and/or having that same location as a superimposed Chamber as described in the section following the explanation of Burrows on page 96.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006112#post1006112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What matters to you isn't distance, but the kind of connection you have to a place. Your Lair serves as a nexus point to any of these locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Lair is your Horror's hunting grounds and you've been contending that hunting in a place gives it no greater degree of sympathy to your Lair than its being dark and/or stormy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you're overlooking how limiting random Pathways are, too. Beasts can either go to a precise location they know of or a random location. That's pretty limiting! </div> </div> </div>The first time, yes. After that, you're looking at a -3 penalty at worst (for both the return trip and subsequent revisits) on a two-Attribute roll when you're playing a Beat-engine incentivized to raise their Attributes on account of their supermode using the best of them, half their discrete powerset using a dicepool of them plus a non-purchased Trait, and their most travel-friendly Satiety Condition removing Lair from their resistance considerations, to say nothing of how Lair Traits explicitly add to the roll \u2014 if you <i>know</i> there's a graveyard where the ground is uneven and poisonous mushrooms grow, you can almost certainly eat the net -1 penalty to come back there on a weekend to terrify the strangers that live there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially as Satchel is correct in that Beasts don't have much stuff to help them blend in with human cultures. But that's not very surprising considering they're nightmare monsters. </div> </div> </div>See Point 4 \u2014 if you're a nightmare monster that exists on the fringes of human culture, the ability to go essentially anywhere at essentially any time defangs the game's principle thematic tension of having to feed on the terror of people around you. Even high-Lair specimens who can pretty consistently maintain a drip-feed of low Satiety through nightmares alone on the virtue of a high dicepool draw their sustenance from within a handful of miles and/or the bounds of a hive, and the Lair 2 murdercrow almost certainly has enough time to refill their Willpower in the time between feedings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, regarding power... Think of this. You're already acknowledging that a Beast can call up a blizzard when they want to. How does that fit in with other supernatural creatures? How powerful is that? </div> </div> </div>A changeling can call up a blizzard with a power that costs three Experiences to learn. A werewolf of the Storm Lords with a single dot of Wisdom Renown can make that same investment to gain the ability to invoke extreme temperatures in line with the local climate. &quot;Create an environmental Tilt, including Blizzard&quot; is an Apprentice-level Forces spell. And while information on 2e is quite a ways off from being available to us in more than general fragments, I don't find it remotely hard to believe that a Sin-Eater with the appropriate Haunt could invoke a blizzard without too much difficulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts have an Atavism that lets them spew out fire for no cost. Beasts are meant to be powerful in their box. But it's still a box and they don't have any of the flexibility Mages can show. </div> </div> </div>It's a box that you've been arguing they can expand merely by using that Atavism or a similarly simple/straightforward method. Every Beast has at least one minor Lair Trait in their arsenal and minor Lair Traits include things like &quot;the lights are flickering and/or dim&quot; \u2014 being able to trivially enter most buildings at night without Atavisms or physical engagement with the security just because your Lair is Poorly Lit is a bit excessive as definitions of &quot;in your box&quot; go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-21-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:04:02-08:00","id":1006384,"title":"","content":"Traits are what defines the resonance of your Lair, and therefore what locations have sympathy to your Lair. To add a Chamber to your Lair, it has to have one of your Lair Traits. This isn't my interpretation, that's just what the book says. I'm not contending anything with this, I'm just citing what the book says here.<br /> <br /> I don't know what else you want to be &quot;resonance&quot; or &quot;sympathy&quot;. I'm not seeing anything else being called out. If you see something, point it out in the book. I'll look at it. But I don't want to get into it with you about interpretations without something concrete that can pointed to that we can both agree on as common ground. <br /> <br /> Without that, we'll just be talking over each other and only irritate both of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:53:52-08:00","id":1006468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006384#post1006384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what else you want to be &quot;resonance&quot; or &quot;sympathy&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did my repeated invocation of &quot;the places that you have seen or done things that echo the creation of your Chambers are substantially easier to bring your Lair Traits into&quot; pass unnoticed somehow?<br /> <br /> Your Lair Traits are the barest connection your Lair has to the wider world besides &quot;your Lair is in a part of the cosmology that notionally connects to every other place in the world.&quot; Your physical experience of a location and the nature of discrete vistas within your Lair offer more concrete connections to locations within a given realm, and the only scaling bridge between those things and Lair Traits is the table under Chambers and Lair Traits. &quot;This place contains elements that are Cramped, Flooded, and Electrified, and so does your Lair&quot; should not have the same degree of connection as &quot;This basement contains elements that are Cramped, Flooded, and Electrified, and you waterboarded a man here until a piece of his mind broke off, just like you did to another man in the basement that forms one of the Chambers of your Lair&quot; \u2014 the latter should definitely be easier to get to than the former, but you're proposing that they have an identical degree of connection to the Lair of a monster who has &quot;a basement where a man was waterboarded until a piece of his mind broke off&quot; as part of its home on the basis of\u2026 a literal and broad reading of Lair resonance and a decision to deliberately ignore the explicit mention of Primordial Pathways in the context of the Chambers and Lair Traits section?<br /> <br /> Expanding your territory via the acquisition of Chambers requires your Lair Traits, which exist as part of your Lair regardless of how many Chambers you actually have, and your physical presence, which requires that you be outside your Lair due to the Horror's refusal/inability to leave the Lair. Extending your Lair Traits into locations where none of them are present requires resonance with one of your Chambers, which you needed at least a temporary instance of one of your Lair Traits to acquire, and your physical presence, for the same reasons as adding a place as a Chamber (along with the fact that you can invoke Lair Traits freely within your Lair), and doing so requires spending a point of Satiety regardless of whether the place is the original location or a substitute. Outside of locations similar to your Chambers, you cannot invoke Lair Traits without the presence of at least one of them in the location, which can only be done once per scene but has no associated cost on its own, and your presence in that location, which is self-explanatory. Opening a Primordial Pathway from outside the Lair most unambiguously requires your presence at the location being bridged with your Lair and is made easier by the presence of your Lair Traits and being in the seed of one of your Chambers and/or in a world whose geography is less rigid than the material realm.<br /> <br /> There's a kind of hierarchy of relevance these things suggest, where your Lair Traits let you set up Chambers and your Chambers let you set up additional shortcuts and your additional shortcuts let you reliably move between points that were once only relevant to your Lair through you being a Beast who was in those places.<br /> <br /> If a Lair Trait is all that is required to temporarily connect your Lair with another location, then either Chambers and Chamber-analogues exist as a weird exception to that rule and suggest no sort of continuum of relevance to your Lair and/or Legend, or Chambers should have a substantially lesser cost associated with invoking Lair Traits from nothing to justify using them over other locations when opening a Pathway \u2014 a single point of Willpower is not supposed to be a more onerous cost than a single point of Satiety, else the benefit Lair resonance provides to Atavisms makes no sense. If even Lair Traits are optional to opening a Primordial Pathway to anywhere, then there is even less reason for Beasts not to jump to the outside edge of their known experiences to feed, given that one of their means of regaining Willpower is to <i>evoke their Legend</i>.<br /> <br /> Again, one of the example characters is in prison, starving, and in danger of being killed by his fellow inmates. Unless he is <i>supremely dense</i>, he has no obvious reason to remain in this desperate state under the interpretation of the mechanics that allows any character to open a Pathway to any place with comparative ease \u2014 even a combined -5 penalty from Starving and being in the material world has at least a one in ten chance of success in allowing him to enter his Lair. (For the record, those odds also possess a ten percent chance that a type of damage will occur that specifically references the relevance of Chambers to the use of Pathways, which is at odds with your repeated claims that Chambers are just parts of the Lair and the outside world that it's easy for you to travel between.)<br /> <br /> My reading is that if you have the Downpour Lair Trait and one of your Chambers is a forest where you once robbed a terrified stranger on a rainy night, then you should be able to more readily move to and from other forests where you have robbed terrified strangers, regardless of whether or not it's raining in any of them, because you're a Beast whose Legend is that of a monster which dwells in rainy places and robs people in forests so long as you have that Chamber. Is this an unreasonable reading, compared to &quot;Any rainy place in the same cosmological neck of the woods is equally easy to move to, because you're something that dwells in rainy places&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T18:40:26-08:00","id":1006497,"title":"","content":"I think I might see where some crosstalking might be occurring... <br /> <br /> First, to clarify, I haven't ignored the deliberate mention of opening Pathways in the Chamber and Lair Traits section. I'm reading the context of where the mention of opening Pathways is in. Chamber and Lair Traits first states that if you're in your Chamber, you can spend Satiety to apply any Lair Traits you're permitted. Then it says that in locations which are similar to a Chamber, you can still try to impose Lair Traits by spending willpower and making a Wits + Resolve roll with a dice penalty based on how dissimilar the location is from one of your Chambers. <br /> <br /> From there, we get each of the degrees of dissimilarity. Note how spiritual dissimilarity starts by saying that a Beast wants to open a Pathway in a different forest from his Chamber. If he recreates the similar circumstances of hunting someone, he makes it more spiritually similar. New sentence, &quot;Spiritual similarity levies a -2 dice penalty.&quot; This dice penalty is strictly for imposing a Lair Traits on the area. Once a Lair Traits is present, then the Beast can use the new resonance from the Trait to open a Pathway, which uses the rules under the section Primordial Pathways, which is another willpower point spent, another Wits + Resolve roll and with a -3 dice penalty for being a location that's other than a Chamber but with +1 die for the Lair Trait.<br /> <br /> These are two different actions, with two different rolls and each have their own modifiers. <br /> <br /> Chambers don't provide resonance, the book states that its Lair Traits which do that. If there are no Lair Traits going on around you already, and you're not in a location that has even a descriptive similarity, then you can't apply any Lair Traits to the area and you're stuck. You can't open a Pathway there. <br /> <br /> This is probably why that Beast prisoner is stuck. He doesn't have appropriate Lair Traits to take advantage of his environment, he doesn't have a prison cell as a Chamber, and he's really restricted in what he can do, so he can't manipulate his environment to create the scenario they need. <br /> <br /> The Imposing Traits section provides an explicit description of how triggering a sprinkler system qualifies for applying the Downpour Trait, which then makes that location resonate for the Makara in the example. <br /> <br /> Considering that a location only needs to be resonant to you in order to open a Pathway.... In your example of a Beast with Downpour and a forest setting Chamber, they could do the same trick with the sprinklers to apply the Downpour Trait and then try to open a Pathway in the building. <br /> <br /> So, I don't think that the prisoner Beast is dense, I think they're stuck because they don't have an applicable Trait to use in their environment, or an applicable Chamber to use to impose a Trait for their location. <br /> <br /> Chambers are incredibly important for a Beast. They provide you with easier access to your Lair and they also provide you with more setting options that you can use for imposing Traits when you need to.<br /> <br /> Frankly, this is why I suggest that if a Player wants to make things &quot;easier&quot; for themselves in accessing their Lair in times of danger, take the &quot;Extreme Heat&quot; Trait, the Dragonfire Atavism and just retreat into a building and burn the place up. Turn the inside into an inferno and you'll get the Extreme Heat Trait applied and then you can open a Pathway to merge with your Horror for a real fight. In a burning building. <br /> <br /> Granted, this isn't a subtle tactic, but it looks legit to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T20:52:43-08:00","id":1006551,"title":"","content":"To point out the problem with this reading:<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that, absent a precise replica of one of your Chambers, the best circumstances you have for a roll to open a Primordial Pathway in a location that is next-most-analogous to one of your Chambers is to dump two points of Willpower into, say, making a basement dark or flooded and opening the connection \u2014 a process that is markedly more involved and resource-intensive than your implicit commonplace option of jumping into a river and making the waters impenetrably dark through the two Traits' connection.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that, following a paragraph which contains the line &quot;Like with A, you can spend a Willpower point to attempt B in a substitute location,&quot; in a list of paragraphs whose ending sentences proceed &quot;This level offers no penalty to A and B,&quot; &quot;This level offers a -2 penalty,&quot; &quot;This level offers a -4 penalty,&quot; &quot;This level offers a -5 penalty,&quot; the lack of greater detail on all the levels after the first means &quot;The penalties for this level apply only to B, not A&quot; instead of &quot;The modifier for this level applies to the same things that the preceding level does.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that opening a Pathway from one of your Chambers when you formed it under unusual circumstances not reflective of its basic state requires a point of Satiety, despite this, again, being markedly more expensive than just finding a specimen of one of your Lair Traits, invoking the rest of them, and opening a Pathway from there, which is a counterintuitive state of affairs.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that, despite one of the Satiety Conditions explicitly giving a moderate bonus to opening Primordial Pathways to and from one of your Chambers and the result of dramatic failure in opening a Pathway expressly being &quot;the Chamber you used for the Pathway disconnects from the rest of your Lair until you can reconnect it,&quot; the only relevance your Chambers have to Primordial Pathways are that you can go out of your way to throw more resources at making simple environmental connections to pave the way for your Horror to pick you up in the sort of place it should notionally be easiest for you to join with it than if you just stumbled across unrelated specimens of those connections elsewhere.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that the Eastside Pyro, who has always needed to burn, cannot torch one of his Chambers to make room for another one, turn a fellow inmate into a man-sized bonfire to the general trauma of onlookers, and expand his Lair into the prison on the strength of fear and fire, when you've just suggested escalating to supernatural arson as a means of rapid preparation for trouble.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that Atavisms like Shadowed Soul and Heart of the Ocean having movement boosters in line with qualities that have associated Lair Traits for comparatively little reason, because if your Horror dwells someplace Flooded or Suffocating or Dark then you can instantly go to any body of water or unlit location with no greater penalty than you'd face from trying to get to your Lair through the invocation of Traits via Chamber similarity.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that invoking Lair Traits pretty much only exists for the sake of characters without certain Atavisms or without complementary/redundant Lair Traits that align with those Atavisms, because if you have Dragonfire or Storm-Lashed and any fire-and-smoke or weather-related Lair Traits then you can daisy-chain any of your other Traits without even rolling, thus turning those two Atavisms into the best escape mechanisms in the game due to the sheer volume of Lair Traits they can cause for anyone who builds their Lair toward those ends.<br /> <br /> You're suggesting that the whole system of &quot;you can spend Willpower instead of Satiety to use one of your Atavisms' Satiety Expenditure effects [Lair] times per scene as long as you're in the vicinity of one of your Lair Traits&quot; is a trap mechanic meant to distract you from the real means of using your Lair Traits to power up, which is to merge with your Horror through the mere presence of a piece of its furniture in a setting.<br /> <br /> You are suggesting, in short, that two points of Willpower and a net +4 to the roll in the material world are the only things incentivizing Beasts to hew close to their Chambers and the circumstances that made those places into chunks of their supernatural soulscape rather than turn themselves into a roiling nexus of storm and fire and darkness that hangs around their hometown getting secretly famous out of mere force of habit.<br /> <br /> It's not very tidy, as mechanical reads go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T21:34:33-08:00","id":1006566,"title":"","content":"I didn't suggest a single thing, Satchel. Those are all your words. <br /> <br /> If you want to have an actual conversation sometime, instead of being snippy, ask and maybe I'll oblige you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T22:05:39-08:00","id":1006580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006566#post1006566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't suggest a single thing, Satchel. Those are all your words.</div> </div> </div> </div>My words include multiple not-uncharitable paraphrases of your words, including &quot;Opening a Primordial Pathway requires only the presence of a Lair Trait corresponding to your Lair; the benefit of a Chamber to making Primordial Pathway rolls is the ability to instantiate your Lair Traits without having any of them present at the time&quot; and take into account the facts that Lair Traits include &quot;there is some manner of fluid in this location that is waist-deep or deeper,&quot; &quot;the geography of this location is difficult to navigate,&quot; &quot;there is a moderately-sized fire in this location,&quot; &quot;this location is as cold as the average walk-in freezer,&quot; or &quot;this location is foggy,&quot; that the presence of one allows you to invoke the others without a roll or expenditure, and that Chambers can be formed in locations that do not normally contain elements that match one of your Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> If you wish to contest my understanding of your interpretation, or any of the things from the books that I brought up \u2014 things that you asked for despite demonstrating a willingness to ignore otherwise clear statements like &quot;your Chambers are relevant to the actual opening of Primordial Pathways, as evidenced by the mention of them in the roll results for the act itself, the use of a direct example of the act in the section on how locations' similarity to Chambers relates to Lair Traits, and the explicit presence of a bonus to use a particular Chamber for them in one of the Satiety Conditions&quot; or interpret them in a manner which is less straightforward than directly implicit but better suits your desired outcome \u2014 then by all means continue to be a drain on my day off, but don't waste my time by saying you're done talking and then talking to me about how you're not interested in talking to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to have an actual conversation sometime, instead of being snippy, ask and maybe I'll oblige you. </div> </div> </div>You and I evidently have very different thresholds for what constitutes an attempt at conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T22:18:26-08:00","id":1006586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006580#post1006580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My words include multiple not-uncharitable paraphrases of your words, including &quot;Opening a Primordial Pathway requires only the presence of a Lair Trait corresponding to your Lair; the benefit of a Chamber to making Primordial Pathway rolls is the ability to instantiate your Lair Traits without having any of them present at the time&quot; and take into account the facts that Lair Traits include &quot;there is some manner of fluid in this location that is waist-deep or deeper,&quot; &quot;the geography of this location is difficult to navigate,&quot; &quot;there is a moderately-sized fire in this location,&quot; &quot;this location is as cold as the average walk-in freezer,&quot; or &quot;this location is foggy,&quot; that the presence of one allows you to invoke the others without a roll or expenditure, and that Chambers can be formed in locations that do not normally contain elements that match one of your Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> If you wish to contest my understanding of your interpretation, or any of the things from the books that I brought up \u2014 things that you asked for despite demonstrating a willingness to ignore otherwise clear statements like &quot;your Chambers are relevant to the actual opening of Primordial Pathways, as evidenced by the mention of them in the roll results for the act itself, the use of a direct example of the act in the section on how locations' similarity to Chambers relates to Lair Traits, and the explicit presence of a bonus to use a particular Chamber for them in one of the Satiety Conditions&quot; or interpret them in a manner which is less straightforward than directly implicit but better suits your desired outcome \u2014 then by all means continue to be a drain on my day off, but don't waste my time by saying you're done talking and then talking to me about how you're not interested in talking to me.<br /> <br /> You and I evidently have very different thresholds for what constitutes an attempt at conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. You should do something enjoyable with your day off instead of doing something you consider a drain. Hope you have a good day. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T00:41:16-08:00","id":1006620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1006586#post1006586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. You should do something enjoyable with your day off instead of doing something you consider a drain. Hope you have a good day. ^.^</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't do that please, it's threadcrapping and adds nothing to the conversation. If you are done speaking with someone then be done with it and move on.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T18:45:14-08:00","id":1006953,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Satchel, please review your point by point addressing of Paradim. Starting off each sentence with &quot;you're suggesting...&quot; comes across as antagonistic, I should have addressed that in my previous post. Please be aware of how your tone may be perceived when formatting your replies so as to avoid this kind of exchange in the future.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:08:02-08:00","id":1015345,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has been suggested so far, but I always found the Wits + Resolve dice pool for opening the Primordial Pathways to be strange and rather small. One possible solution would be to change it to Resolve + Occult + Lair, and come up with a quick high Lair Merit that lets you gain an Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T20:12:19-08:00","id":1015504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1015345#post1015345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has been suggested so far, but I always found the Wits + Resolve dice pool for opening the Primordial Pathways to be strange and rather small.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not the only one who uses it and the ability to link places to a patch of real estate in a dimension of sensory-feedback through similar observable qualities is more a function of imagination and concentration than application of esoteric variables and mystical gravity. The Pathway's dicepool gets bigger in direct proportion to the length it stays open prior to exceptional success and the overlap method is by design the least secure means of entry available to characters even before accounting for the capacity to hand out spare keys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T01:32:04-08:00","id":1019131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways#post1001311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the 'Accessing Your Lair' section, and the really horribly placed and named 'Chambers and Lair Traits' section, the total dice penalty for trying to open a Pathway from a place similar to your chamber (ie, graveyard to graveyard) is -8.<br /> <br /> If you recreate the circumstances under which you formed the original chamber perfectly, it's still -5 (-3 for material world, not the location of chamber, and -2 for Spiritual similarity).<br /> <br /> This is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Are people actually playing with these penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as the back of the book doesn't refer to the traits modifiers effecting moving through primordial pathways to your lair, and it is not written or referred to in the open the primordial pathway section, I don't use it in my games. I did try briefly after reading on here that some interpret it differently, but the multiple tables and referencing seems unnecessary, missplaced and not intended. <br /> <br /> So no, not everyone uses the 'double penalty's as they're mechanics written for two different abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T09:22:16-07:00","id":1249156,"title":"","content":"Maybe it s of little use to post on a discussion so old but...<br /> Does anybody noticed that the core book states that the hive TRAIT give the apex the ability to open a pathway in every chamber of the lair?<br /> And on the players guide it states that a beast cannot open a pathway to a chamber that hasn t a TRAIT in common with the beast lair","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T22:48:10-07:00","id":1250660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways#post1001311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the 'Accessing Your Lair' section, and the really horribly placed and named 'Chambers and Lair Traits' section, the total dice penalty for trying to open a Pathway from a place similar to your chamber (ie, graveyard to graveyard) is -8.<br /> <br /> If you recreate the circumstances under which you formed the original chamber perfectly, it's still -5 (-3 for material world, not the location of chamber, and -2 for Spiritual similarity).<br /> <br /> This is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Are people actually playing with these penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I open Pathways all the time. As others have said, just do it from your Chamber's physical location, and it costs nothing willpower-wise; just takes time. Your Chamber's physical analogue must have at least one Lair Trait in effect anyway, so that knocks off the -3 instantly and makes it at the very least +1 on the roll (For a single Lair Trait). Make sure you go from chamber's physical analogue to the chamber itself and the -3 penalty for 'specified a world but not a specific location' goes away, too. Even with Wits 2 and Resolve 2 that's an easy 5 dicepool, and since you're not burning a Willpower to even attempt it you could use use one for 3 extra dice if you wanted to get 8 dice total; it's very unlikely you'd not get even a single success on that roll, and also as others have said you could just keep trying with 5 dice until you succeed.<br /> <br /> Outside a Chamber's physical location you have it a great deal rougher, but that's why you try to find or create conditions that match your Lair Traits if you need your full power in a pinch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T23:00:46-07:00","id":1250662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1250660#post1250660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Chamber's physical analogue must have at least one Lair Trait in effect anyway, so that knocks off the -3 instantly and makes it at the very least +1 on the roll (For a single Lair Trait).</div> </div> </div> </div>Your prospective Chamber's physical analogue needs at least one Lair Trait in effect during the time that the Chamber was formed, which is not necessarily a consistent feature of the physical location (the physical seed of the Chamber you got from staging a blackout raid isn't immune to daylight, for example) and the actual origin site of a Chamber already gives a +1 to the roll on top of changing out the -3 penalty for opening a Pathway to the material world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even with Wits 2 and Resolve 2 that's an easy 5 dicepool, and since you're not burning a Willpower to even attempt it you could use use one for 3 extra dice if you wanted to get 8 dice total; it's very unlikely you'd not get even a single success on that roll, and also as others have said you could just keep trying with 5 dice until you succeed. </div> </div> </div>The roll costs 1 Willpower regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T22:44:11-07:00","id":1251568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1250662#post1250662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your prospective Chamber's physical analogue needs at least one Lair Trait in effect during the time that the Chamber was formed, which is not necessarily a consistent feature of the physical location (the physical seed of the Chamber you got from staging a blackout raid isn't immune to daylight, for example) and the actual origin site of a Chamber already gives a +1 to the roll on top of changing out the -3 penalty for opening a Pathway to the material world.<br /> <br /> <b>The roll costs 1 Willpower regardless.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtPpage97</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can\u2019t simply open Pathways between any realms they<br /> choose. As with many aspects of their Lair, it\u2019s the resonance,<br /> or similarity, between the Lair and somewhere else that affords<br /> access. <b>Opening a Pathway to the exact location from which<br /> the Beast created a Chamber is easiest, but desperate Beasts<br /> and cunning would-be intruders can use similar locations<br /> by spending a point of Willpower during the attempt and<br /> incurring an additional dice penalty based on how well the<br /> location matches.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>No, it does not according to the highlighted section above, which strongly suggests that in the Chamber's physical location you just have to make the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T23:11:21-07:00","id":1251573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1001311-prohibitive-penalties-for-opening-primordial-pathways?p=1251568#post1251568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it does not according to the highlighted section above, which strongly suggests that in the Chamber's physical location you just have to make the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Update your PDF and look again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.